hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15031","(15031) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; He did not combine the seven rak'ahs, and he prayed two rak'ahs for each week."
"15032","(15032) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: I saw Arak bin Malik praying every week. Two rak'ahs"
"15033","(15033) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There are two rak’ahs for every week, of which neither a voluntary rak’ah nor a voluntary prayer is sufficient. obligatory"
"15034","(15034) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Ata was asked about game that was taken at large and slaughtered. The sanctuary? He said: Al-Hasan bin Ali, Aisha, and Ibn Omar hated him."
"15035","(15035) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos; They hated for game to enter the sanctuary and then be slaughtered there."
"15036","(15036) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; He did not see anything wrong with hunting that is permissible in the Haram, or eating it that is permissible in the Sacred Sanctuary. He said: He was Ibn Abbas hated it."
"15037","(15037) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a gift if it is damaged. To sell it and use its price for another gift."
"15038","(15038) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said about a man who had intercourse with his Umrah, then had intercourse with his wife before completing his Umrah. He said: He is repeating his Umrah. And He guides the body."
"15039","(15039) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers; Concerning a man who took the ihram for his life, then had intercourse with his family before he circumambulated the Kaaba, saying: He will return to where he entered ihram. Then he will be forbidden, and blood will be shed."
"15040","(15040) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a mahram has intercourse with his wife, and she is a mahram. By two ‘umrahs, he said: He will give a gift for each of them, and they will continue for their two ‘umrahs."
"15041","(15041) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders; He was asked about a man who had an intercourse with his wife, then had intercourse with his wife before he reached home? He said: They will return to each other and fulfill their lives, and they will separate until they have finished their lives, and upon them both This is my religion"
"15042","(15042) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: He must return to the time, and he will be rewarded. With his life and shedding of blood."
"15043","(15043) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen; When Al-Hussein bin Ali entered ihram, he would anoint himself with oil, and he would anoint his companions with perfume, or he would apply perfume on their body."
"15044","(15044) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to anoint it with oil before entering ihram."
"15045","(15045) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to apply oil when entering ihram."
"15046","(15046) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; When entering ihram, he used to apply oil, meaning oil."
"15047","(15047) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Farqad Al-Sabkhi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to apply oil when entering ihram, other than what is abhorrent, meaning perfume. (Ahmad 29. Ibn Khuzaymah 2652)"
"15048","(15048) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Five animals. There is no blame on the one who kills them while it is forbidden. The mouse, the scorpion, the crow, the kite, and the squirrel dog. (Bukhari 1826. Muslim 76)"
"15049","(15049) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar: What animals should a person in ihram kill? He said: One of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he commanded By killing the mouse, the scorpion, the squirrel dog, the kite, and the crow. (Bukhari 1827, Muslim 75)"
"15050","(15050) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: Sa`id bin al-Musayyab said: Five people will kill them. Muharram; The scorpion, the snake, the wolf, the crow, and the dog."
"15051","(15051) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Minqar Abi Basham, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: No. There is no harm in killing a snake and throwing a camel. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I found in another place: Bishr abi bashama, with this chain of transmission, and he said: He means the forbidden."
"15052","(15052) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Abraham: Should a person in ihram kill a mouse? He said: No."
"15053","(15053) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He kills the Fuwaisiqi."
"15054","(15054) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and on the authority of Mughiry, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The person in ihram should not kill anyone. The wild beasts, except for what is wrong with him."
"15055","(15055) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Every enemy who is against you, kill him while you are in Ihram."
"15056","(15056) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I passed by snakes while I was in ihram. So I killed them with a stick that I had with me. When I came to Omar, I asked him about their killing? He said: Kill them, for they are the enemy."
"15057","(15057) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar was asked about killing a snake while he was Forbidden? He said: Kill them."
"15058","(15058) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: We were with Ibn Umar while we were in ihram, and we saw a snake. Then Salem came to us and killed her."
"15059","(15059) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the hyena, if it attacks a person in ihram, let him kill him. If he kills him before he attacks him, then he must make an old sheep."
"15060","(15060) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; He said: The Muhrim kills the snake, the scorpion, the wild beast, the squirrel dog, and the fox. It was said to him: Why was it said about fuisqa? He said: Because the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up with her, and she had taken a wick with which to burn the house."
"15061","(15061) Mahboub narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The pilgrim in ihram kills the mouse and the crow. The magpie"
"15062","(15062) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Let the Muhrim kill a mouse, a scorpion, a kite, a crow, and a gnawed dog.\n(Muslim 857. Ahmad 6/231)"
"15063","(15063) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace; Similarly, it added: And he kills the snake. (Muslim 67 Ahmad 97)"
"15064","(15064) Abdullah bin Nimir told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard him say: Five. So, kill them in the sanctuary. The kite, the crow, the dog, the mouse, and the scorpion. (Muslim 66. Ahmad 6/209)"
"15065","(15065) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: There is no blame on you if You kill them while you are in sacred state."
"15066","(15066) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul A’la, on the authority of Suwayd bin He ignored him and said: Omar ordered us to kill the snake and the hornet while we were in ihram."
"15067","(15067) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kulayl, on the authority of Tawus, who said: No, you should not call it Hajj. Not even a lifetime, the intention is sufficient for you."
"15068","(15068) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If you want to enter ihram, do not say anything, but Whatever your intention is, whether Hajj or Umrah."
"15069","(15069) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Your intention during Hajj is sufficient for you. And the Umrah, if you want to enter ihram."
"15070","(15070) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: I performed Hajj with some of Abdullah’s companions, but they were not named. Until they share"
"15071","(15071) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The intention is sufficient."
"15072","(15072) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who made Hajj and Umrah obligatory, but he did not speak about them? He said: He did not want to, but he intended, and he commanded him to name him."
"15073","(15073) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq, the servant of the family of Omar, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: It is sufficient. The intention"
"15074","(15074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The intention is sufficient."
"15075","(15075) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Shahr, who said: There is no harm for the person in ihram to wash his clothes. And he commanded her to be washed, but he hated to wash her himself."
"15076","(15076) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram taking a bath. And he washes his clothes."
"15077","(15077) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to bathe without ritual impurity. And he washes his clothes."
"15078","(15078) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to wash his clothes."
"15079","(15079) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: God does not do anything about your turbidity. Something"
"15080","(15080) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram taking a bath. And he washes his clothes."
"15081","(15081) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He said: Should a person in ihram wash his clothes? He said: Yes."
"15082","(15082) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A person in ihram should apply kohl with any Kohl is fine, as long as there is no good in it."
"15083","(15083) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Aisha ibn Talhah, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers; She disliked for a woman in ihram to use kohl with anticonvulsant."
"15084","(15084) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a person in a state of ihram has ash, let him apply kohl, but not It is applied with something good in it."
"15085","(15085) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Mujahid: Do you apply antihmad to a muhrim? He said: No, I said: There is nothing good in it. He said: There is something good in it."
"15086","(15086) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: A woman in ihram should wear whatever Any type of clothing, whether eastern or western, but do not use kohl with anti-corrosion."
"15087","(15087) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, saying: I asked Jabir bin Zayd about a woman in ihram applying kohl. By antimony? His thoughts"
"15088","(15088) Ibn Mahdi told us, he said: Zayd bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of his leaders, he said: A woman asked Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr and Ibn Omar, on the authority of a woman in ihram who applied kohl with antimony? So Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr ordered her to shed blood."
"15089","(15089) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not apply kohl except with ash, and do not apply kohl with kohl. It is good."
"15090","(15090) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who reaches the time and is unconscious, he said: He will perform the prayer on his behalf."
"15091","(15091) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: May God bless him, meaning the one who passed out."
"15092","(15092) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; That Ali saw a game animal with some of his companions while they were in ihram, so he did not order them to send it."
"15093","(15093) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you enter ihram and you have some game, leave it alone. On his way"
"15094","(15094) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: We were We perform Hajj and leave with our families some game items, which we do not send."
"15095","(15095) Hafs told us, he said: I asked Ibn Jurayj: What Ata used to say about a man who goes out, and he was left behind in his house? Some of the hunting, so something happens to it? He said: He guarantees."
"15096","(15096) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Hassan ibn Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he enters ihram And he has some game in his hand, so let him send it to him."
"15097","(15097) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he enters ihram and there is a bird in his hand So let him send him"
"15098","(15098) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The child, if he performs Hajj, the slave, if he performs Hajj, and the Bedouins, if he performs Hajj. If he performs Hajj, and then the Bedouin immigrates, and the child has a wet dream, and the slave is freed, then they must perform Hajj."
"15099","(15099) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The pilgrimage of the slaves is like this. And so on, then he was freed, and he had to perform Hajj."
"15100","(15100) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The child and the slave are obligated to perform Hajj, and the Bedouins are obligated to perform Hajj. Hajj is sufficient, because Hajj is prescribed for him wherever he is, and whoever performs Hajj is among the Bedouins."
"15101","(15101) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I heard a sheikh speaking to Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I want to bring new content into the hearts of the believers, whether or not you are a child. His family performed Hajj with him, then he died, that will suffice for him, and if he realizes that, then Hajj is required of him, and whenever he is a slave, his family performs Hajj with him, then He dies, that is sufficient for him, and if he is freed, then Hajj is required. (Abu Dawud 134)"
"15102","(15102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Muhammad, Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb; A woman went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a boy, and she said: O Messenger of God, is this Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded."
"15103","(15103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A Bedouin is sufficient for Hajj."
"15104","(15104) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: It was said: Perform Hajj with them while they are young. If they die, they will have performed Hajj, and if they live, they will have performed Hajj."
"15105","(15105) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said, “Guard from me, and do not say: Ibn Abbas said: Whatever is a slave with whom his family performed Hajj, and then was freed, he must perform the Hajj, and whatever is a boy with whom his family performed Hajj as a child. Then he realized the Hajj of a man, and any Bedouin performed the Hajj of a Bedouin, then he emigrated, so he did the Hajj of a migrant. (Ibn Khuzaymah 3050)"
"15106","(15106) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They believed that the woman If she performs Hajj and there is a child in her womb, then it is permissible for him to perform Hajj."
"15107","(15107) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When he performs Hajj He is a Bedouin, and the Hajj of Islam is sufficient for him."
"15108","(15108) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: He met a group of spirits, and said: Who are the people? They said: Muslims. They said: Who are you? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then a woman picked up a young boy and said: Is this Hajj? He said: Yes, and you will be rewarded.\n(Muslim 4091 Abu Dawud 1733)"
"15109","(15109) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is sufficient on behalf of a minor. Hajj until he grows up."
"15110","(15110) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He does to a boy in ihram what is done to a man. He is protected from wearing perfume, circumambulated with him, performed with him in ceremonies, and performed on his behalf."
"15111","(15111) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, the same, except that he said: They may not pray on his behalf, even if they wish. They cropped it, and if they wanted to, they would not have cropped it."
"15112","(15112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; That Abu Bakr circumambulated Ibn al-Zubayr in a rag."
"15113","(15113) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar (h) and on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha; They used to gather the boys during Hajj, and circumambulate them between Safa and Marwa."
"15114","(15114) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A boy should avoid anything during ihram. He avoids major things from adornments and perfumes."
"15115","(15115) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And we answered on behalf of the children."
"15116","(15116) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He used to enter ihram for boys, and strip them at the arrival of the new moon."
"15117","(15117) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: Urwah used to perform Hajj as a child, and he would perform the rituals with them. When entering ihram."
"15118","(15118) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sanded from stone to stone three times, and walked the rest of the way, except that Wakia did not say: All of that"
"15119","(15119) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Spring Omar bin Al-Khattab sanded between stone to stone."
"15120","(15120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Hisham; Verily, Urwa is sand from stone to stone."
"15121","(15121) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul;"
"15122","(15122) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I entered with Al-Qasim, and he braked three times, and walked between the two corners."
"15123","(15123) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he came to Mecca for Hajj or Umrah, he would make three circumambulations of the House and walk four times, and he would say: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do. (بخاری ۱۶۱۷۔ مسلم ۲۳۱)"
"15124",""
"15125","(15125) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed three times and walked four times."
"15126",""
"15127","(15127) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, that it is sand. Three times and he walked four times."
"15128","(15128) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, who said: I used to sand three stones until Al-Hijr, so our sheikhs came and said: Walk between the two pillars. Among them are Saeed bin Jubayr, Peacock, Mujahid, and Ata."
"15129","(15129) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Tawoos; He was sanding from stone to stone."
"15130","(15130) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sanded from stone to stone. (Muslim 886. Ahmad 3/340)"
"15131","(15131) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan (H) and on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever abandons Tawaf Al-Sadr should do it. Blood"
"15132","(15132) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos, who said: Omar used to return those who went out, but it was not the last of his promise. At home"
"15133","(15133) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, who said: Whoever flees and does not say goodbye, there will be a bloodshed on him."
"15134","(15134) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not see any harm in stoning the Jamarat, washing himself with marshmallow before shaving it."
"15135","(15135) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If shaving is permissible for you, then wash your head as you wish."
"15136","(15136) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm for a pilgrim in ihram to wash his head before To shave"
"15137","(15137) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. He said: I asked them: Should I wash my head? Before I shave, if my throat is sore? They said: Yes, and if you wish, you can wash it with marshmallow."
"15138","(15138) Hammad bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab Ja’far bin Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it for a man to wash his head with marshmallow before shaving it."
"15139","(15139) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; He dislikes a woman washing her head with hibiscus, meaning if she wants to cut her hair."
"15140","(15140) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to wash his head with marshmallow before shaving it. He said: He was a generous person and hated it."
"15141","(15141) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man said to Ibn Abbas: Does a man ride a fat woman? He said: Not heavy. He said: So he milks it? He said: Not Mujahid."
"15142","(15142) Abu Malik al-Janabi Amr ibn Hashim told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali, who said: He rides The man I treated him with kindness."
"15143","(15143) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man needs a physical vehicle, let him ride it."
"15144","(15144) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah; Regarding the body, he said: Ride it without stumbling."
"15145","(15145) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man driving his body, and he said : Ride it. He said: It is a body. He said: Ride it."
"15146","(15146) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Ride the sacrificial animal in a reasonable manner, until you find a back. (Muslim 961, Abu Dawud 1758)"
"15147","(15147) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mujahid; {Therein are benefits for you until an appointed time.} He said: In its buildings and its outbuildings, and in its outbuildings until it is called a body. So if it is called a body, then it refers to the Ancient House."
"15148","(15148) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He rides it and carries on it."
"15149","(15149) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, he said: Ride it, he said: Indeed, it is a body. He said: Ride it without breaking it."
"15150","(15150) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said about the body, he said: If he is in need Her driver gave her a ride without a fat loss, and he drank the surplus from nurturing her two children."
"15151","(15151) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In the body, if you need a back, you ride, and you carry it on her with kindness."
"15152","(15152) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man driving his body, and he said: Ride it. He said: It is his body. He said: Even if She was fat.\n(Bukhari 1689 and Abu Dawud 1757)"
"15153","(15153) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man driving his body or his animal, and he said: Ride it. He said: It is His body, or his gift, he said: even if it is.\n(Muslim 374. Ahmad 3/167)"
"15154","(15154) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ajlan Mawla al-Mish’al, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man driving his body, and he said: Ride it. He said: It is his body, he said Ride it and woe to you, or woe to you."
"15155","(15155) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, On the authority of Mujahid, he said: If he needs milk, he drinks, if he needs to ride, he rides, and if he needs wool, he takes it."
"15156","(15156) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted them to ride it if they needed it."
"15157","(15157) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Do not ride a body, nor carry anything on it. Except for a matter for which you will not find a substitute, nor will you drink of its milk unless you become a widow."
"15158","(15158) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Kanood, on the authority of Abdullah; Concerning a man who frees his female slave and marries her. He said: He is like a rider on his camel."
"15159","(15159) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ride it.\n(Bukhari 1690, Ahmad 3/231)"
"15160","(15160) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who frees his female slaves, then Will he marry her? He said: He is like a rider on his body."
"15161","(15161) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife before visiting the house, he said: There is blood on her."
"15162","(15162) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: If it happens before he is visited, he should do it. Body"
"15163","(15163) Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’; Concerning a man who performed all of the rituals except circumambulation of the Kaaba, then he went to his family, and they said: On him is his body, and he completed Hajj"
"15164","(15164) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he falls before he visits, then his body is upon him. And Hajj from before."
"15165","(15165) Ibn Fudayl and Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Humaid, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, a man ignorant of the Sunnah, far from wretchedness, and meek. I performed all the rituals, except that I did not I visited the House until I fell in love with my wife, and he said: My body, and Hajj from Qabil. So he repeated it three times, all of that. He says: Physically, and Hajj from before."
"15166","(15166) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; Concerning the one who has intercourse with his wife before he visits the house, he said: He has a physical obligation."
"15167","(15167) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man Did he have intercourse with his wife before he visited the house? He said: On him and his wife."
"15168","(15168) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: If he falls before he visits, then he must perform Hajj from He met"
"15169","(15169) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He is obligated to perform the Hajj, and he will sacrifice it."
"15170","(15170) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyy, on the authority of Yahya bin Salem, he said: I and a man from Banu I spoke to Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, and he said: A man who performed all the rituals, and when it was the Day of Sacrifice, he came upon his family before To visit, he said: He has a physical obligation, and he did not say: He has to perform Hajj from a future person."
"15171","(15171) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; In Muhrim, he falls before circumambulating the Kaaba. He said: They will complete their Hajj, and each one of them will shed blood. Hajj is obligatory upon them both from before."
"15172","(15172) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will shed blood, and he must perform Hajj from He met"
"15173","(15173) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah al-Bariki, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He is required to perform Hajj from Qabil. I said: What if he performed Hajj from Oman? He said: Even if he performs Hajj from Oman."
"15174","(15174) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ikrimah and Ata’; They said about a man having intercourse with his wife before he visits the house. They said: It is upon him to have physical intercourse with him."
"15175","(15175) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is brave, and his Hajj has been completed."
"15176","(15176) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Dhar, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not use lice while you are in ihram."
"15177","(15177) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He scratches his head with the pad of his fingertips."
"15178","(15178) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram scratching his head gently."
"15179",""
"15180","(15180) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; That a man said to Ibn Abbas while he was performing Hajj while he was in ihram: Should I scratch my head while I am in ihram? So Ibn Abbas gathered all his hands together, rubbed his head with them, and said: As for me, I say like this, so the man said to him: Do you see? If I kill a lice? He said: I stayed away, and the lice did not prevent you from scratching my head, and you were only forbidden from hunting."
"15181","(15181) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair; He heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: With the pads of his fingertips, saying about a muhrim scratching his head. He said: And tell me who He saw Omar telling a story."
"15182","(15182) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Regarding a Muhrim scratching his head, he said: Yes, he scratches it with his fingertips."
"15183","(15183) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, who said: I said to him: I heard Ibrahim but he did not see it. Is it wrong for a muhrim to scratch his head? He said: Yes."
"15184","(15184) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I saw Ibn Umar scratching his head while he was Muharram, so I looked and saw him scratching it with his fingertips."
"15185","(15185) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: There is no harm in scratching his head. And it is forbidden."
"15186","(15186) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He scratches it lightly."
"15187","(15187) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sadiqa, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; Concerning a man who shaved his head before he slaughtered. He said: A ransom must be paid. He said: So I asked Mujahid, and a peacock? They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"15188","(15188) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever performs part of his Hajj Or he delays it, then let him shed blood for that reason."
"15189","(15189) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Whoever begins his Hajj something before something else, or He shaved his head before he was slaughtered, and there was blood on him that he shed."
"15190","(15190) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he shave before he slaughters, he will shed his hair for that reason. blood, then he recited: {And do not shave your heads until the guidance reaches its place}"
"15191","(15191) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: Whoever innovates anything during his Hajj does not He should sacrifice a sacrifice for that purpose."
"15192","(15192) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever offers part of his Hajj in place of another, there is no blame."
"15193","(15193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; like him\n(Abu Dawud 1932. Ahmad 3/326)"
"15194","(15194) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Isa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; If God wills, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Did I shave before I slaughtered? He said: Then slaughter it and there is no harm in it. He said: Did I slaughter before stoning the stone? He said: Shoot and do not be embarrassed. (Bukhari 83. Tirmidhi 916)"
"15195","(15195) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ayyash, on the authority of Zayd bin Ali, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; A man came to him and said: I cut my hair before I shave. He said: So shave, or cut your hair and do not be embarrassed. (Tirmidhi 885. Ahmad 1/76)"
"15196","(15196) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did I throw stones after the evening? He said: There is no harm, and he said: Did I shave before I slaughtered? He said: There is no harm.\n(Bukhari 1735. Abu Dawud 1976)"
"15197","(15197) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ziyad bin Allaqah, on the authority of Asama bin Sharik; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a man who shaved his head before he slaughtered? He said: There is no harm. (Abu Dawud 2008)"
"15198","(15198) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked about a man who slaughters before shaving? He said: There is no harm. (Bukhari 1734, Muslim 950)"
"15199","(15199) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir; That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about advancing and delaying Hajj? He said: There is no harm. (Nasa’i 4105. Ahmad 3/385)"
"15200","(15200) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Zayd, who said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulating the Kaaba three times, then He sat and was resting, and a servant of his went to us, then he got up and started his tawaf."
"15201","(15201) Muhammad bin Musar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Should I be comfortable during tawaaf, should I sit? He said: Yes."
"15202","(15202) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in a man resting in his quest if he circumambulated between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah without confinement."
"15203","(15203) Waki’ told us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him resting. The man between Safa and Marwa."
"15204","(15204) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Wasiti, who said: I saw Al-Hasan resting. Between them, I mentioned it to Mujahid, and he thought about it."
"15205","(15205) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, identified the body that He was a guide"
"15206","(15206) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no guidance except what is imitated and made known. And he stopped with his knowledge."
"15207","(15207) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, he said: I performed Hajj with Al-Aswad and with him. A lot of sacrifice, so he came to Aisha and asked her? I saw him behind him with something he did not recognize."
"15208","(15208) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I saw Al-Qasim driving his camel to the parking lot."
"15209","(15209) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: He sent for Aisha and asked her: Is he known as physically? He said: She said: Yes, he said: He said: Do you feel? He said: She said: If you wish, it was only made known so that it would be known that it was his body."
"15210","(15210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabah ibn Abi Ma’ruf, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever wishes will know, and whoever wishes will not. He knows, but they knew the dangers of theft."
"15211","(15211) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who left his body with semen and did not make it known. He said: That is sufficient for him, but it was astonishing for him to make it known."
"15212","(15212) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: He sent Abdullah with me to guide him, He said: If it is the evening that he is recognized, then he will be recognized."
"15213","(15213) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Whoever gives a sacrifice and has it known to him. With it"
"15214","(15214) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, on the authority of Salem, who said: Ibn Omar entered into ihram for his life, then he walked Then he said: Hajj and Umrah are nothing but the same. I bear witness that I have made Hajj obligatory with her."
"15215","(15215) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man said to him: I stripped Hajj, should I join it for a lifetime? He said: Yes, and slaughter a ram."
"15216","(15216) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Hajj is added to Umrah, and the Umrah should not be added to Hajj."
"15217","(15217) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos, or one of them; Concerning a man who completed the Hajj, they said: If he wishes, he may perform a lifetime with him, so he will perform the Hajj, and he will give a sacrificial animal."
"15218","(15218) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikki, Ata’, and Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Mecca, he received the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner, but he did not receive Other pillars. (Tabarani 12)"
"15219","(15219) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: I have realized our sheikhdom; Ibn Abbas, Jabir, Abu Hurairah, and Ubaid bin Umair do not receive anything except the Black Stone and the Rukn. They receive other pillars."
"15220","(15220) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, who said: I saw Suwayd ibn Ghafali. He takes over all the pillars of the house."
"15221","(15221) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ali bin Umayyah, he said: When Hajj Omar received the pillar, and Ali bin Umayyah was receiving all the pillars, so Omar said to him: O Ali, what are you doing? He said: I accept all of it, because nothing from the House is abandoned. He said: Then Omar said: Have you not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings be upon him, did not receive anything from it except the stone? He said: Yes, he said: What is worse for you? He said: Yes. (Tabarani 5049)"
"15222","(15222) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He rarely left the Black Stone. And the Yemeni Pillar, unless they touch them during the Witr tawaf."
"15223","(15223) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The two pillars that fill the stone do not... They receive it."
"15224","(15224) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father; He saw Mu'awiyah circumambulating the Kaaba, so he touched all the pillars, and said: There is nothing of it that is forsaken."
"15225","(15225) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, on the authority of his father; He saw that Ibn al-Zubayr did it, and he said: There is nothing wrong with it."
"15226","(15226) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: No. Something is saved from the House."
"15227","(15227) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to touch all the corners, seal them with them, and stick his stomach, back, and sides to the house."
"15228","(15228) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; He returned to the stone and touched it, meaning after the two rak'ahs."
"15229","(15229) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed three times and walked four times, then he came to the place of Abraham and recited: {And take a place of Abraham was praying, so he made a place between him and the House, then he returned to the corner and greeted it."
"15230","(15230) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he prayed the two rak'ahs, he would return to the Hijr and touch it, or face it, say takbeer, then go out to Safa."
"15231","(15231) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: I saw him do that."
"15232","(15232) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: When you come to the House, pick up the stone if you are able. upon him, and you mentioned God, and you prayed for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then you prayed two rak’ahs at the Maqam, or whatever he wanted. God, then turn towards your face and touch the stone. Otherwise, face it and remember God, then go out to Al-Safa."
"15233","(15233) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to return to Al-Hijr and touch it, then go out to Al-Safa."
"15234","(15234) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sara, who said: I saw Salim circumambulating the Kaaba, then He prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, then returned to the Hijr and touched it, then went out to Safa."
"15235","(15235) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you wish, return to Al-Hijr after the two rak’ahs. And if you wish, do not return to it."
"15236","(15236) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A woman came to Ibn Abbas. She said: My mother died and she had to perform Hajj. Should I perform it on her behalf? Ibn Abbas said: Was your mother in debt? She said: Yes. He said: How did you do it? She said: I made up for it on her behalf. Ibn Abbas said: God is the best of your creditors."
"15237","(15237) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Abu Razin Al-Uqaili; He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my father is old and unable to perform Hajj. And the Umrah, nor the Za’an. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah. (Tirmidhi 930, Ahmad 4/11)"
"15238","(15238) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, my father is old and unable to perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, so perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"15239","(15239) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said about the great sheikh, he said: He prepares a man At his expense, he will perform Hajj on his behalf."
"15240","(15240) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father; Ibn Al-Zubayr used to reside in Mecca for years, performing the crescent of Hajj during the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah."
"15241","(15241) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: The crescent has been seen. Then the crescent took its place in Dhul-Hijjah, and when it was in the next year, it was said to him: The crescent has been seen, and it is in House, so he took off the garment that he was wearing, then he performed the crescent moon. When it was the third year, it was said to him: The crescent moon has been seen, so he said: What I am but a man from among my companions. I do as they do. He remained lawful until the Day of Tarwiyah."
"15242","(15242) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: Omar: O people of Mecca, why do I see you in debt, while the pilgrim is disheveled and dusty? When you see the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah, perform the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah."
"15243","(15243) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Quza’ al-Bailili, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He performed the crescent moon in Mecca when he saw the crescent moon."
"15244","(15244) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Umar came and circumambulated, then ran, Then he made it permissible, and stayed for four or five days, then he performed the Hajj on the tenth, then he came another time and made it permissible, until... It was the Day of Tarwiyah. He completed the Hajj when he set off with his camel to Mina. Ata’ said: He is more beloved to us."
"15245","(15245) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, He said: Yahullah on the Day of Tarwiyah."
"15246","(15246) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid; Ilal Ibn Umar was the last of them on the Day of Tarwiyah."
"15247","(15247) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He may have circumambulated, then prayed the two rak'ahs inside the house."
"15248","(15248) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim, who said: I saw him walking around, then entering the House. He prays the two rak'ahs."
"15249","(15249) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: My father was asked about prayer in The Kaaba? He said: I prayed with my father, Hussein bin Ali, in the Kaaba."
"15250","(15250) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the Kaaba, and Asama bin Zaid, Bilal, and Uthman bin Talha, and he stayed there. He remained in the house for a long time, then Ibn Umar entered after him, the first of the people. I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? And peace be upon him? He said: Between the two columns in front. He said: And I forgot to ask him how many times he prayed? (Muslim 391, Abu Dawud 2018)"
"15251","(15251) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uthman. Ibn Talhah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the two rak’ahs and came to you when you entered. (Ahmad 3/410, Talisi 1365)"
"15252","(15252) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray the noon and afternoon prayers, and the sunset and evening prayers, until he came at the end of the night. The house"
"15253","(15253) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid bin Rashid, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Mujahid; They prayed the noon prayer on the Day of Delegation, and behind the back."
"15254","(15254) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; That his father used to pray the noon prayer on the Day of Delegation in Mecca."
"15255","(15255) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father, He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the expedition in Al-Abtah, so Bilal gave the call to prayer at noon, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"15256","(15256) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is Sunnah for the imam to pray the noon prayer on the day of departure. With the simplest."
"15257","(15257) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray to the front of the House, and there was nothing between him and tawaaf. Then Abu Bakr after him, then Omar, then Omar sent him back to the appointed time."
"15258","(15258) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, who narrated it, saying: He came to the Ka’bah, touched the pillar, and brake. Three times, he walked four times, then he advanced to the place of Abraham and recited: {And take the place of Abraham as a place of prayer}, so he made the place Between him and the House."
"15259","(15259) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqamiya recited the Qur’an one night, then circumambulated At home for a week, then he came to the shrine and prayed there."
"15260","(15260) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He was not permitted to abandon prayer at the Maqam, if not You overcame him until you overcame him, or with his shoes, and there is no problem if there are men between you and him. They pray after you have finished your journey."
"15261","(15261) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He liked it to perform the two rak'ahs of Tawaf behind the Maqam, and he saw nothing wrong with that if he did not do so."
"15262","(15262) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Zakaria ibn Abi Zayd, on the authority of Amer; He heard Wahb bin Al-Ajda’, that he heard Omar say: When a man comes for Hajj, he should circumambulate the House seven days, then pray at the shrine. Two rak'ahs"
"15263","(15263) Abdă told us, on the authority of Salih ibn Hayyan, who said: I performed the first circumambulation with Anas ibn Malik, and when he finished he bowed. Two rak'ahs at the Maqam."
"15264","(15264) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he finished his tawaf, he would come to the shrine and pray two rak’ahs there."
"15265","(15265) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He prays two rak’ahs at the Maqam, or whatever he wants. God"
"15266","(15266) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; He circumambulated, then he came to the Maqam, and he prayed two rak’ahs there."
"15267","(15267) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Pray the two rak’ahs of Tawaf in your house if you wish."
"15268","(15268) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr circumambulating the Kaaba. Then he came to pray and circumambulate between him and the qiblah."
"15269","(15269) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Kathir, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of his grandfather; He saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying near the gate of Banu Saham, not between him and the tawaf. A curtain, and people pass through it.\n(Ahmad 6/399, Abu Ali 7137)"
"15270","(15270) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Kathir bin Kathir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abu Wada’i, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah. (Ahmad 399. Tabarani 687)"
"15271","(15271) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: Tawaf for strangers is more beloved to me than prayer."
"15272","(15272) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked whether tawaaf is better, The mother of prayer? He said: As for the people of Mecca, it is prayer, and as for the people of Egypt, it is tawaf."
"15273","(15273) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’? He said: As for you, it is tawaf, and as for the people of Mecca, it is prayer."
"15274","(15274) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I heard Mujahid say: Praying for the people of Mecca is better."
"15275","(15275) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Dharr, who said: I heard a mujahid saying: Prayer for the people of Mecca is better, and tawaaf For those with better prospects."
"15276","(15276) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: I said to him: Did your father raise his voice? By reciting the talbiyah? He said: Explain that."
"15277","(15277) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Talbiyah is the symbol of Hajj. So recite the Talbiyah often at every honor and at every time, and recite the Talbiyah frequently and show it."
"15278","(15278) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Furat, he said: Ibn Abi Maliki said to us: Are you in ihram? We said: Yes, he said: So they responded."
"15279","(15279) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the one who responds, he said: He hears whoever follows him."
"15280","(15280) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked: What is the righteousness of Hajj? He said: Al-Ajj, and the snow."
"15281","(15281) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: I was with Ibn Umar and he turned away so that I could hear what was between them. The two mountains"
"15282","(15282) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Zaid, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, they do not reach the souls until their voices become hoarse due to the intensity of their response."
"15283","(15283) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hazzam ibn Hisham, on the authority of his father; Omar used to recite the Talbiyah on al-Safa and al-Marwah, and his voice was strong, and his voice was known at night, but his face could not be seen."
"15284","(15284) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Khallad Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gabriel came to me and ordered me to command my companions to raise their voices. With God's grace (Tirmidhi 829. Ahmad 4/55)"
"15285","(15285) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Raise Your voices are talbiyah. On the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, similar to that."
"15286","(15286) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Khallad ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Janni, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We are coming. Gabriel, peace be upon him, said: Order your companions to raise their voices in the Talbiyah, for it is the symbol of Hajj.\n(Ahmad 5/192. Ibn Hibban 3803)"
"15287","(15287) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Yazid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja`far al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The best Hajj: Hajj and snow.\n Al-Ajj: the one who performs the Talbiyah, and Al-Thajj: the slaughter of the body. (Tirmidhi 2998)"
"15288","(15288) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, they would raise their voices in reciting the Talbiyah, until their voices became louder, and they would sacrifice to the sun when They entered into ihram."
"15289","(15289) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr waking up people from the people of Yemen in the mosque. And He says: Stand up and respond, for the beauty of Hajj is the Talbiyah."
"15290","(15290) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: The beauty of Hajj. Talbiyah"
"15291","(15291) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: It was Ibn Al-Zubayr says: Talbiyah is the adornment of Hajj."
"15292","(15292) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The symbol of Hajj is the Talbiyah."
"15293","(15293) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: The people of Mecca do not have sand, nor does anyone Anyone from it, unless one of the people of Mecca comes from outside."
"15294","(15294) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was not a widower when he arrived from Mecca."
"15295","(15295) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, who said: May Allah reward us, me and Bakr from Mecca. So we went around the House and made sand."
"15296","(15296) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, who said: Ata’ was asked about the neighbourhood, when he entered ihram from Mecca, whether he would perform the sa’y rounds. The three? He said: They are striving. As for Ibn Abbas, he said: That is only for the people of the horizons."
"15297","(15297) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Harb ibn Surayj, or Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: He is not responsible for the people of Mecca. Sand"
"15298","(15298) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no sand on the Day of Sacrifice."
"15299","(15299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I saw him laying sand on the Day of Sacrifice."
"15300","(15300) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no sand in the circumambulation of annexation."
"15301","(15301) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Bura ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: It was mentioned to Ibn Umar al-Talbiyyah on the day He recognized her and said: I prefer takbeer."
"15302","(15302) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, that he said: Cut off the Talbiyah when you go to Arafah. And Glory be to God."
"15303","(15303) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, he said: I was with Ibn Masoud recognized my heart, and a man said: Who is this, this day? Then Ibn Masoud turned to her and said: Here you are, as many as the dust. Here you are."
"15304","(15304) Ibn Fudayl and Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: We went in the morning with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Minna to Arafat, and some of us said the Great and some of us called the Talbiyyah.\n(Abu Dawud 1812. Ahmad 2/22)"
"15305","(15305) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas with his knowledge. He says: O God, may God help you."
"15306","(15306) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was mentioned to him that Mu'awiyah forbade the Talbiyah, so he came until he took hold of the two pillars of the tent, then he recited the Talbiyah, then said: He knew that Ali was He is reciting the Talbiyah on this day, so he liked to differ from it."
"15307","(15307) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibrahim, Labybi Ibn Masoud with his knowledge, and it was said: Who is this? Al-Mallabi? It was said: Ibn Masoud, but they remained silent."
"15308","(15308) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded. And he was standing at Arafat."
"15309","(15309) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, who said: I was walking with Ibn Umar and Ibn al-Hanafi from from one to the other. Arafat, Ibn Umar used to say takbir, and Ibn al-Hanafiyyah used to say Talbiyya."
"15310","(15310) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: I asked Anas: How did you deal with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He used to recite the Talbiyah, but he would not be denounced for it, and he would say “Allahu Akbar”, but he would not be denounced for it. (Bukhari 970 and Muslim 933)"
"15311","(15311) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed ibn Jubayr, and Ata’; They used to pray in the Sacred Mosque, and they would perform Hajj when they left the mosque, and they would delay tawaf."
"15312","(15312) Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mu’mil, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Maliki tawaf At the House and between Safa and Marwah, before he left for Minna."
"15313","(15313) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, who said: I asked Salim about a man entering ihram for Hajj who circumambulates before he He goes out, or after he returns? He said: It is like religion. As long as you hasten, it is better."
"15314","(15314) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, he said: I asked Al-Qasim bin Muhammad about him? He said: All of that is good."
"15315","(15315) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say: Tawaf between Safa and Marwa is for the people of Mecca, after they return from Mina."
"15316","(15316) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba, and he threw seven pebbles at it. He says “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble."
"15317","(15317) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zayd, he said: Abdullah threw a stone. Jamrat al-Aqaba is from the depths of the valley. He says “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble."
"15318","(15318) Mahboub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khalqani, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah throwing pebbles at Al-Aqaba. From the depths of the valley, he says “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble."
"15319","(15319) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who had two pebbles fall at the Jamarat, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar” with each one of them."
"15320","(15320) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble, “Allahu Akbar.”"
"15321","(15321) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his mother; She saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, go deep into the valley and throw seven pebbles at the Jamarat, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each one. pebble"
"15322","(15322) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba and said “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble."
"15323","(15323) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Gabriel, peace be upon him, gave Abraham gave seven pebbles, then they set off for Al-Aqaba, and Satan appeared to them and said to him: Throw and say “Allahu Akbar.” He said: So they threw them. And they said “Allahu Akbar” with each stoning, until Satan stopped, then he did the same thing with the other two Jamarat."
"15324","(15324) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He did not give permission for not opening the Black Stone. He concludes with it the first circumambulation he performed on the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Departure."
"15325","(15325) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; It was astonishing for him to receive the stone when it was opened and when it was sealed."
"15326","(15326) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to bring the Black Stone and seal it with it, then his family would come to it."
"15327","(15327) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, who said: I heard Ibn Sabit saying of a man who did tawaf and wanted to He takes possession of the Yemeni Corner and begins with it. Ibn Sabit said: Do not start from the beginning of the black, if you begin your tawaf."
"15328","(15328) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he said: You will receive peace in every instance if you are able to do so. Otherwise, it opens and ends with it."
"15329","(15329) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you are able to touch yourself in every tawaf, then touch it. Otherwise, when you pass by it, face it and say “Allahu Akbar,” and if you wish, open with it and conclude."
"15330","(15330) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maimunah, who said: I saw a man walking around, and when he came to a stone He said “Allahu Akbar” and begins with it and ends with it."
"15331","(15331) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, started with the Black Stone, and moved from stone to stone."
"15332","(15332) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the call to prayer. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We passed by the house, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, walked around it and then left before he left. In the morning"
"15333","(15333) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man reaches the place of abjection, let him put down his mount, then Whoever visits the House, let him leave it, if he wishes, by night, and if he wishes, during the day, after he has descended in it and put on his shoes."
"15334","(15334) Abu Muti’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He finishes everything he has, so if there is nothing left Nothing but riding, then circumambulating the Kaaba, then proceeding."
"15335","(15335) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated to build around He is building the Kaaba and supervising it."
"15336","(15336) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: They hated to build a building. At Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and they lengthen it so that the House appears to them."
"15337","(15337) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa and Saeed bin Jubayr. They say: The greatest Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice."
"15338","(15338) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni, on the authority of Shihab bin Abbad Al-Asri, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: The greatest Hajj is the day of Arafah. So I mentioned it to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: I tell you on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar said: The greatest Hajj The Day of Arafah"
"15339","(15339) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad about the greatest day of Hajj? He said: It was a day on which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Hajj and the people of religious faiths performed the Hajj."
"15340","(15340) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Shaddad about the greater Hajj? He said: The greatest Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice."
"15341","(15341) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The greatest day of Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice."
"15342","(15342) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali; That a man met him on the Day of Sacrifice, and he took his bridle and asked him about the greater Hajj? He said: This is today."
"15343","(15343) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of A camel, and he said: This is the Day of Sacrifice, this is the Day of Sacrifice, and this is the day of the Greater Hajj."
"15344","(15344) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The greatest Hajj is the day on which blood is shed. And the forbidden is permissible therein."
"15345","(15345) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, and Ayyash al-Amiri They heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The greatest Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice."
"15346","(15346) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The greatest Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice."
"15347","(15347) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Juhaifah, who said: The greatest Hajj is the day of Hajj. The slaughter"
"15348","(15348) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man asked him, He said: My father died and never performed Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, for if you do not increase his goodness, you will not increase his evil."
"15349","(15349) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, who said: I was sitting with Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab when a man came to him and said: My father struggled a lot and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? Then Saeed said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had granted a man permission to perform Hajj on behalf of his father, and is it anything but a debt?"
"15350","(15350) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Qadamah bin Abdullah Al-Rawasi, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about a brother. Because he died and never performed Hajj, should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Did he leave behind any children? He said: I said: No, except a young boy. He said: Hajj on his behalf, for if he had found a messenger, he would have sent to you to hasten her. I said: Should I perform Hajj on his behalf from my own wealth, or from his wealth? He said: No, but from his money. And I asked Abraham about him? He said: Perform Hajj on his behalf. He said: I asked Al-Dahhak? He said: Perform Hajj on his behalf, for that will suffice on his behalf, and perform Hajj from his wealth."
"15351","(15351) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of a man called: Yusuf. It will be with Ibn Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, my father died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Are you his eldest son? He said: Yes, he said: So he performed Hajj on behalf of your father. Do you think that if your father had a debt, you would pay it off?"
"15352","(15352) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He performs Hajj on behalf of the dead, even if he does not He advises you"
"15353","(15353) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: No one should perform Hajj on the authority of No one, and no one should fast on behalf of anyone else."
"15354","(15354) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No one should perform Hajj on behalf of another."
"15355","(15355) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: No one should perform Hajj on behalf of anyone else."
"15356","(15356) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Hajj is not made up for the dead."
"15357","(15357) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If only I had given alms on his behalf, And I guided you."
"15358","(15358) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Labid, who said: Shurayh said: If you With your Umrah and Hajj, then you arrive at Mecca, and nothing unlawful will be permitted from you until the Day of Sacrifice, for they will say to you: If you circumambulate For your Umrah and Hajj, it is permissible, so do not obey them in that."
"15359","(15359) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Al-Hussein bin Ali and Shurayh joined each other, and neither of them entered the ihram until the Day of Sacrifice."
"15360","(15360) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Nasr; Ali said to him: Take them both together, and when you reach Mecca, perform two circumambulations for them. A circumambulation for your Umrah, and a circumambulation for your Hajj, and do not permit anything unlawful from you except the Day of Sacrifice."
"15361","(15361) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: What did you say when you made Hajj obligatory? He said: I said: Oh God, I declare it as a sacrifice for what Your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, claimed. He said: If he has a gift, it is not permissible. What is forbidden from you? He said: So all of the people were permitted and shortened their hair, except for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whoever was with him as a guide."
"15362","(15362) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Urwa; That Abu Bakr and Omar were arriving and they were full of Hajj, but none of them were permitted to perform anything unlawful until the Day of Sacrifice."
"15363","(15363) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever enters ihram for both Hajj and Umrah One circumambulation is sufficient, and it is not permissible until he has completed his Hajj, and it is permissible for both of them."
"15364","(15364) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abu Shu’ba, he said: I was next to Ibn Umar with his knowledge. And my knees touch his knees, or my thighs touch his thigh, so I have not heard anything more than these words; There is no god, no, God is alone, with no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is powerful over all things, to the point that He surpasses those who know Him. To the plural."
"15365","(15365) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, who said: I stood with Salim bin Abdullah With your knowledge, see how it is done? He continued in remembrance and supplication until the people flocked to it."
"15366","(15366) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I multiply my supplications, and the supplications of the prophets before me, with my knowledge; There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. O God, make My heart is light, and there is light in my hearing, and there is light in my sight. Oh God, expand my chest for me, and make my affairs easy for me, and I seek refuge in You from obsessive thoughts. The chest, the dispersion of affairs, and the temptations of the grave. O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what enters in the night and the evil of what enters in the day. And the evil of what the winds blow.\n(Tirmidhi 352, Ibn Khuzaymah 2841)"
"15367","(15367) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Arabi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: I multiply my supplications and the supplications of the prophets before me with my knowledge. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. In His hand is goodness. He gives life and causes death. He is powerful over all things."
"15368","(15368) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: I told him: What What is the best thing to say during our Hajj? He said: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"15369","(15369) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sadiqa ibn Yasar, who said: I asked Mujahid about his reciting the Qur’an. The best day of Arafah, or the remembrance? He said: No, but rather the recitation of the Qur’an."
"15370","(15370) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shattar, who said: I told Ibn Hanafi: What is the best thing we should say during our Hajj? He said: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"15371","(15371) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man, from Bakr bin Wa’il, who said: I asked Ibn Umar, I said: In this regard, we deny Hajj, and some people claim that there is no Hajj for us. He said: Do you not perform the Hajj and circumambulate the Kaaba? And between Safa and Marwah, and you throw stones at the Jamarat, and you stand at the parking lot? They said: Yes. He said: You are pilgrims. A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about something like that. You asked me about him and he did not answer until these verses were revealed: {There is no blame upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord} So he called him and recited it to him, then said: You are pilgrims.\n(Abu Dawud 1730, Ahmad 2/155)"
"15372","(15372) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came to him A man, and he said: I sacrificed myself to a people and withheld from them some of my reward for the sake of Hajj, so will that suffice? About me? Ibn Abbas said: This is one of those whom God Almighty said: {Those will have a share of what they have earned, and God is quick in reckoning}"
"15373","(15373) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a hired worker who rents himself out to Mecca, then gives permission. He said: It is sufficient for him."
"15374","(15374) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Concerning the merchant and the runaway, they said: It is sufficient for them both."
"15375","(15375) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan Abu Taloot, on the authority of Abu Al-Salil, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a man who forces himself to perform Hajj, he said: It is sufficient."
"15376","(15376) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Dhar, he said: I asked Mujahid about the merchant, the worker, and the employee? He said: The worker does not detract from his Hajj, nor does the merchant take away from his Hajj, nor does the hired worker detract from his Hajj."
"15377","(15377) Abu Nu’aym and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I heard him and a Bedouin asked him, and he said: I forced camels and I wanted to perform Hajj. Will that be sufficient for me? He said: No, no honor."
"15378","(15378) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It is not sufficient."
"15379","(15379) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, who said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: There are people Do they claim, or who among them claims, that there is no Hajj for Karai? He said: Rather, he will perform a beautiful and beautiful Hajj, if he fears God, fulfills his trusts, and is a good companion."
"15380","(15380) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, in the Almighty’s saying: {So fasting for three days. Days during the Hajj} He said: Fast the day before the tarwih, the day of the tarwiyah, and the day of Arafat. On the night of measles, he fasted for three days, and for seven days when he returned."
"15381","(15381) Ibn Fudail, Iyad, and Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: The last one. The Day of Arafah"
"15382","(15382) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I heard Abu Ja`far say: The last day is the Day of Arafah."
"15383","(15383) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he wishes, he may fast the first and middle days of the ten days, and the last day. He knew"
"15384","(15384) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, similar to what Ata’ said."
"15385","(15385) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The last day is the day of Arafah."
"15386","(15386) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: Al-Hakam and I went to Abu Al-Walid, and he informed us that he had heard Ibn Omar says: The last day is the Day of Arafah."
"15387","(15387) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, in the Almighty’s saying: {Fasting for three days during the Hajj} He said: One day before the narration and the last day is the day of Arafah."
"15388","(15388) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, similarly."
"15389","(15389) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever does not fast the day before the Tarwiyah, And on the Day of Tarwiyah, and on the Day of Arafah, he missed fasting."
"15390","(15390) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Ubaid bin Umair, who said Ibn Umar: The day before the day of Tarwiyah, the day of Tarwiyah, and the day of Arafah, and he said: Ubaid bin Umayr: He fasts The days of the East."
"15391","(15391) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus, and Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He makes The one who performs tamattu ends his fast on the Day of Arafah."
"15392","(15392) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {Fasting for three days during the Hajj} the last of which is the day He knew"
"15393","(15393) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: The last day is He knew"
"15394","(15394) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The sick person is carried to the pyre, if he is able to If he throws stones, let him throw them, and if he is not able to do so, let him put the pebbles in his palm, then throw them from his palm."
"15395","(15395) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: All rituals will be witnessed by the sick person, and he will be circumambulated. With it on a loader, when he throws the stones, it is placed in his palm, then he is thrown with it from his palm."
"15396","(15396) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He throws stones from his head."
"15397","(15397) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman should not perform Hajj except with a mahram."
"15398","(15398) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said: You will go out in company, including men and women."
"15399","(15399) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: You perform Hajj with a group of men and women, and you take a ladder to ascend. upon her, and let not hatred bring her near."
"15400","(15400) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad Abi Hubaira, who said: A woman from The people of the Lord went to Abraham. She was well-off and had neither a husband nor a mahram, and had never performed Hajj. So Abraham wrote to her: This is from the path that, God said, “And you do not have a mahram, so do not perform Hajj except with Baal, or a mahram.”"
"15401","(15401) Jarir told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah, he said: Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan used to grant permission to a woman who did not perform Hajj. Never perform Hajj with a woman who is a mahram with her."
"15402","(15402) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: A woman shall not travel for a period of three days or more except with her mother, or her son, or her father, or her brother, or Her husband, or a mahram. (Abu Dawud 1723, Tirmidhi 1169)"
"15403","(15403) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, that he was asked about a woman who wants to perform Hajj and her husband. He was absent in Khurasan, and he said: If it is the obligatory duty and she has a mahram, then there is no problem."
"15404","(15404) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: A woman should not perform Hajj except with a husband, or a mahram."
"15405","(15405) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul-Ala, who said: Ikrimah was asked about a woman performing Hajj with Other than a mahram or a husband, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a woman to travel for more than three days except With a mahram, what should you do with his wife?"
"15406","(15406) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said : A woman should not travel for more than three days except with a mahram. (Bukhari 1087, Muslim 713)"
"15407","(15407) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, delivered a sermon saying: No woman should travel except with a mahram. Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, your wife has gone out. Hajj, and I was registered for such-and-such’s expedition, so he said: Go and perform Hajj with your wife.\n(Bukhari 3006 and Muslim 978)"
"15408","(15408) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It was mentioned to Aisha that a woman should not travel except with a man. A mahram. Aisha said: Not all women find a mahram."
"15409","(15409) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No woman should travel a full day’s journey except with a mahram. (Bukhari 1088 and Muslim 977)"
"15410","(15410) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, who said: It was mentioned to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, a woman who traveled with Her servant thought about that, and it was said to him: He is her breastfed brother, but he did not see any harm in it."
"15411","(15411) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ata’, about a man who is granted ihram with two proofs. He said: He is a mutatitu."
"15412","(15412) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He has to perform Hajj and Umrah."
"15413","(15413) Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying to Ibn Al-Zubayr when the sun went down: Spread out."
"15414","(15414) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that Gabriel came to Ibrahim and stopped at Arafat, and even if it was as hasty as anyone prays Maghrib, he pushed it away."
"15415","(15415) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly."
"15416","(15416) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: I was informed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah. Ibn al-Muttalib, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed Arafat and said: As for what follows, this is the day of the greatest Hajj, and The pre-Islamic people and the idols used to pay off on this day before sunset, when the mountains were darkened. It is as if they were the turbans of men on their faces, and we will repel after sunset, so do not hasten us, our guidance is contrary to the guidance of the people of Polytheism and idols."
"15417","(15417) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim that he heard Ibn Al-Zubayr say: The imam is the one who knows when the sun sets."
"15418","(15418) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to see the defense of those who knew him. When the night approaches and the fasting person breaks his fast."
"15419","(15419) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, who said: I stood with Abdullah, and Othman was in charge of the people, until when the sun had set. He said: If the Commander of the Faithful had continued the hour, he would have reached the age. His words were not too quick and eloquent."
"15420","(15420) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to desire that when they entered Mecca they would not leave. Until they complete the Qur’an."
"15421","(15421) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It would amaze them when they came to Mecca on Hajj. Or command them not to go out until they have recited what they have of the Qur’an."
"15422","(15422) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He loved, or It is recommended that if he comes to any of these mosques, he does not leave until he has read the Qur’an, in the Sacred Mosque and the Mosque Medina and Bayt Al-Maqdis Mosque."
"15423","(15423) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, that he recited it, meaning the Qur’an wherever it was presented. Mecca"
"15424","(15424) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya Al-Bakai, who said: Ibn Umar heard a man reciting while he was circumambulating the Kaaba. He ended it"
"15425","(15425) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He used to hate reciting the ten verses in tawaf, but He remembers God and praises Him and glorifies Him."
"15426","(15426) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata, who said: The Qur’anic rite in Tawaf is modern."
"15427","(15427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, who said: I circumambulated with Sa’id ibn Jubayr, and he did not stop mentioning God"
"15428","(15428) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about the Qur’an women performing tawaf around the Kaaba, but he did not see anything wrong with it."
"15429","(15429) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: I saw our companions reciting Mujahid during the Tawaf."
"15430","(15430) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he was The reciters hate it during tawaaf."
"15431","(15431) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that he was with Ibn Umar, so he went to a group and prayed. Maghrib, then he turned to us and said: The prayer is united, and he did not separate between them."
"15432","(15432) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I performed Hajj with Abdullah, when a group of people came, he called the call to prayer and said the iqama, and he prayed the Maghrib prayer three times, then he had dinner, then he called the call to prayer and said the iqama and prayed the evening prayer. Two rak'ahs"
"15433","(15433) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, that Umar did Like what Ibn Masoud did."
"15434","(15434) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Dhib, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, gathered them together, and did not perform voluntary prayers between them. (Abu Dawud 1921, Malik 196)"
"15435","(15435) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and Othman bin Talhah and Bilal, so they stared at the door for a long time, then they opened, and I was the first of the people to enter. So I met Bilal and said: Where did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? He said: Between the two columns in front."
"15436","(15436) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in the House. He turned towards him when he entered him.\n(Muslim 391. Ibn Khuzaymah 3017)"
"15437","(15437) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: Should I pray in the outskirts of the house? He said: Yes, pray in any direction you wish."
"15438","(15438) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Safwan, or Ibn Safwan, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs in the House when he entered it."
"15439","(15439) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: In the eggs of ostrich there is a dirham in each egg."
"15440","(15440) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: “The value of ostrich eggs is their value.”"
"15441","(15441) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidy, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: In the eggs of ostrich Its value"
"15442","(15442) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: “The value of ostrich eggs is their value.”"
"15443","(15443) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Dhakwan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked On the authority of a Muhrim who caught ostrich eggs, he said: He saw that in every egg he had to fast a day, or feed two poor people."
"15444","(15444) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Similar to the hadith of Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Juraij."
"15445","(15445) Waki’ and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said, “The value of ostrich eggs is their value.”"
"15446","(15446) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Ubaid Allah, who said: I asked a peacock about the whites of a partridge. Muhrim, he said, “It is worth it.”"
"15447","(15447) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said about ostrich eggs that a forbidden man pointed to as permissible: Fasting for a day, or feeding a poor person."
"15448","(15448) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: In every two eggs A dirham, and in every egg there is half a dirham."
"15449","(15449) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Omar, that he said about eggs. Its value"
"15450","(15450) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, that a man had intercourse He found an ostrich egg, so he asked Ali, and he said: You owe a she-camel for every egg that you kill, or a female fetus, so he went to the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him what he said: He said: He said: I did not hear, and you must fast a day in every egg. Or feed a poor person. (Ahmad 5/58, Bayhaqi 207)"
"15451","(15451) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Its price."
"15452","(15452) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Fasting for a day, or feeding poor people."
"15453","(15453) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Lahiq bin Hamid, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, that Ibn Masoud said about that: For every egg you have to fast a day, or feed a poor person."
"15454","(15454) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam about the eggs of the sanctuary doves, and he said: In their eggs is a mudd of food."
"15455","(15455) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ikrimah, that[corrupt] A man came to him and asked him about a man who slaughtered a male child. He said: There was blood on him."
"15456","(15456) Abu Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is blood on him."
"15457","(15457) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the body it produces, he said: He will carry it on it, and if he slaughters it and eats it, he will slaughter a ram in its place."
"15458","(15458) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was carrying a child. The body is upon her."
"15459","(15459) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A fat child must be slaughtered with his mother."
"15460","(15460) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say: If the female body is slaughtered, its offspring are slaughtered. With her"
"15461","(15461) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about a man who drove his camel and it fell on the road, and it fell. He can carry it, he said: He can do with it whatever he wants, so when he enters Mecca, he slaughters a ram in his place."
"15462","(15462) Ibn Abi Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: Will you please stop by your knowledge before the imam? He said: No."
"15463","(15463) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he narrated Before the imam."
"15464","(15464) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, who said: A friend of ours spoke before the Imam, so I asked. Struggling, he said: Shedding blood."
"15465","(15465) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he utters blood before the imam, he will have to shed blood."
"15466","(15466) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, about a man who passed by a crowd without seeing it. Stopping until he came from me, he said: This sheds blood."
"15467","(15467) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding someone who was ignorant to spend the night with a crowd. He said: He shed blood."
"15468","(15468) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard him say: Whoever vomits, on the authority of the plural, he did not He will cause it to shed blood."
"15469","(15469) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever does not stand with a plural, makes it A lifetime"
"15470","(15470) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever does not stand with a crowd, there is no Hajj for him, and he may perform Hajj from He met"
"15471","(15471) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: One reward."
"15472","(15472) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: One reward."
"15473","(15473) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If they participate and his companions do not ransom him, then he must pay the ransom. All of it"
"15474","(15474) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: One reward, and Mujahid said: Indeed. They ate from it, and each one of them has a recompense."
"15475","(15475) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id, who said: There is a recompense for each one of them."
"15476","(15476) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: There is a reward for each one of them."
"15477","(15477) Jarir narrated to us on the authority of Mughirah, and Ibn Shubarmah on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: If they join together, then each one of them must do so. reward"
"15478","(15478) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If they both eat from it, then each one of them must be rewarded, and if not If they eat, they will both have one reward."
"15479","(15479) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far and Ata’ about people who participate in hunting while they are hunting. They are forbidden, so he said: one penalty."
"15480","(15480) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the two men participate in the hunt, then it is expiation. One, and if they both eat, then each one of them will be recompensed."
"15481","(15481) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is a reward for every human being among them."
"15482","(15482) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was asked about a people of the infantry who were killed. Sidon, he said: They have one reward."
"15483","(15483) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: He used to say, “If two people attack Sidon, then the One upon them."
"15484","(15484) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: There is a reward for every one of them, and he said: Hammad. One reward is sufficient for both of them. He said: So I told Al-Harith what Al-Sha’bi said. He said: The statement is what Hammad said."
"15485","(15485) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: “Everything of hunting is governed by people of justice.”"
"15486","(15486) Ibn Abi Ghaniyā narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Everything that is afflicted by a person in ihram is game. Therein is a just government."
"15487","(15487) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to slaughter manna, but not pray. The two rak'ahs."
"15488","(15488) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I asked Ata’, I said: Abd al-Karim said to me, in Mani: Do not slaughter until You pray. He said: This is not upon my family, but rather upon the people of the horizons. I asked Mujahid, and he told me the same thing."
"15489","(15489) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: I asked Ata’, someone said to me: Pray the two rak’ahs before you slaughter. He said: This does not apply to my family, but rather their prayer is their position as a whole."
"15490","(15490) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, Tawoos, Ata’, Salem and Al-Qasim, they said: No prayer. With Mina on the Day of Sacrifice."
"15491","(15491) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad said that they prayed two rak'ahs with manna on the Day of Sacrifice before they performed the sacrifice."
"15492","(15492) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said the two rak’ahs It is obligatory for the one who slaughters before he does it, and the one who does not sacrifice must perform it, and he claims that he does not prostrate. They kissed them when they broke the fast, nor did they offer the sacrifice."
"15493","(15493) Abdul-Ala bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of His mother, she said: It is as if I have been looking at Ali on the mule of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for days before me and he is calling: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: These are not days of fasting, rather they are days of eating and drinking.\n(Ahmad 92. Ibn Khuzaymah 2147)"
"15494","(15494) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah bin Omar in Minna, so we came With food, his son stepped aside and said: I am fasting. He said: Eat, for these are days of eating and drinking. He said, so he broke his fast."
"15495","(15495) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The days of Tashreeq are days of taste and remembrance."
"15496","(15496) Hafs and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I asked Abraham about fasting on the days of Tashreeq. He said: Masruq said: These are the days of eating and drinking."
"15497","(15497) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Bedil bin Al-Khuza’i’s paper on a camel with leaves proclaiming, “Days of misfortune.” Indeed, these are days of eating and drinking. (Tabarani 423)"
"15498","(15498) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: A man from the Ansar, from the companions of the Messenger of God, narrated to me. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me in the days of Tashreeq and he commanded me to call out to the people. These are days of eating and drinking."
"15499","(15499) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Bishr ibn Suhaim, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delivered a sermon during the days of Tashreeq, and said: No one will enter Paradise except a believing soul. And these days are days of eating and drinking. (Ahmad 4/3351 Darami 1766)"
"15500","(15500) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Mundhir bin Jahm, on the authority of Omar bin Khalda Al-Ansari, on the authority of His mother, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Ali to announce the days of Tashreeq. These are days of eating, drinking, and livelihood.\n(Abdullah bin Hamid 1562)"
"15501","(15501) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We used to fast on the days of Tashreeq with Mina, then we were prohibited from doing so."
"15502","(15502) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr and Salem, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Abdullah bin Hudhafi, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called out the days of sunrise, for they are days of eating. And drink.\n(Nasa’i 2876. Ahmad 3/450)"
"15503","(15503) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The days of Tashreeq are days of eating and drinking. (Ibn Majah 1719. Ahmad 2/229)"
"15504","(15504) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Malih, who said: The days of Tashreeq are days of eating. And drink."
"15505","(15505) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The Day of Arafah, the Day of Sacrifice, and the Days of Tashreeq are the feast of the people of Islam, and these are days of eating and drinking."
"15506","(15506) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of a man, called: Jesus, that Ali granted permission It is permissible for a person in ihram to imitate his camel."
"15507","(15507) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, or Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: There is no harm in a person in ihram immigrating his camel."
"15508","(15508) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram slaughtering his camel."
"15509","(15509) Abbad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Abdullah bin Hadir said: I saw Omar ibn al-Khattab watering his camel while he was in ihram and putting it in the mud."
"15510","(15510) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who unties his camel and throws worms off of him and makes him dream. He said: : Monkey, fly, and throw worms off your camels."
"15511","(15511) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: A man said to Ata’: Should I sacrifice my camel while I am in ihram? He said: Yes, Ibn Umar did that."
"15512","(15512) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Al-Darda’, I asked: Mujahid, about a muhrim in ihram slaughtering his camel? He said: No problem."
"15513","(15513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he disliked having his camels slaughtered."
"15514","(15514) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he disliked the camel’s slaughter. Ibn Abbas said: He slaughtered her, he said: So we slaughtered her, and he said: How many ticks or goblins did she kill on her skin?"
"15515","(15515) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athai: A person in ihram ties his camel and slaughters it. With tar."
"15516","(15516) Ibn Uyaynah and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas? He said: There is no harm in it."
"15517","(15517) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, he said: Abu Al-Zubair narrated to us that he heard Jabir bin Abd God says: There is no harm in a person in ihram immigrating his camel."
"15518","(15518) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmaliya, he said: I killed a tick or a wasp while I was in ihram, so Ibn Saeed: Give dates in charity. He said: Dates are better than that."
"15519","(15519) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: I asked a man about ticks that were afflicted by a Muhrim. He said: A date is better than a tick. Rather, half a date, or even a stone, is better than a tick."
"15520","(15520) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi in Muharram who kills a tick. He said, “He feeds a palm of Wheat food, flour, or dates."
"15521","(15521) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Muslimama, who said: I heard Ikrimah being asked about a muhrim who killed a dreamer. He said: He gives in charity his broken pieces."
"15522","(15522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He will be judged in error. And intentionally."
"15523","(15523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is judged in error. And intentionally."
"15524","(15524) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: The reward was only made in Intentionally, but be harsh on them regarding the error so that they may fear."
"15525","(15525) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Intentionality and error in hunting are the same, it shall be judged. Aliyah"
"15526","(15526) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Omar was written to judge him in error. And intentionally."
"15527","(15527) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Taman, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Umar like him."
"15528","(15528) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I was informed, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said: He who is correct will not be judged. He hunted intentionally. Only he who made a mistake will be judged. I was informed, on the authority of Tawoos, that he said: He who made a mistake will not be judged. An error, but the one who did it intentionally is judged guilty."
"15529","(15529) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, Al-Qasim, Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, they said: So If he struck grasshoppers or lizards, he was not convicted of a mistake, but if he struck them intentionally, he was convicted."
"15530","(15530) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Madinah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not upon him. There is something wrong with it."
"15531","(15531) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Mistake and intentionality in hunting are the same, it shall be judged. Aliyah"
"15532","(15532) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will be judged in cases of error and intentionality."
"15533","(15533) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw Al-Hasan hastening to Mina one day ahead of the people. And I saw Hisham hastening."
"15534","(15534) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about rushing to Mina a day before Tarwiyah, but he did not see That's a shame."
"15535","(15535) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah, who said: I asked Ata’, and he said: Like that."
"15536","(15536) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I was with Salim, and with Abdullah bin Ubaid. By God, I did not see them washing the pebbles of the pebbles."
"15537","(15537) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri: Should I wash the pebbles of the pebbles? He said: No, unless there is dirt in it."
"15538","(15538) Al-Aqdi Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: Al-Qasim used to wash the pebbles for the pebbles. And he takes it as it is and throws it away."
"15539","(15539) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Murea’ bin Musa, he heard a sheikh narrating that he saw Sa’id bin Jubayr washing The pebbles of the pebbles."
"15540","(15540) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata’, and he said: Do not wash it."
"15541","(15541) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to wash the pebbles of the pebbles."
"15542","(15542) Ma’an bin Issa narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, who said: By God, indeed The prayer must be made up, but how can the stoning of stone not be made up?"
"15543","(15543) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed With his she-camel, he rode on it, and when she set off, his camel met him."
"15544","(15544) Ma’n narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad arriving when his mount set out with him. From the courtyard of Dhul-Halifiyah Mosque."
"15545","(15545) Ma’n told us, on the authority of Khalid, that he saw Salim doing the same thing."
"15546","(15546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in Dhul-Halifah Mosque. When his camel reached the courtyard of the mosque, it was occupied. (Malik 29)"
"15547","(15547) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was when it was sent My camel returned, and Aisha did not return until she came to the desert. (Bukhari 1553, Muslim 27)"
"15548","(15548) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, who said: They used to love to recite the Talbiyah when his camel sat with it. Standing"
"15549","(15549) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Raja’, that when Alqamiya sat on the camel He began to recite the Talbiyah, and you recited it while he was reciting the Talbiyah."
"15550","(15550) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, when he places his foot in the place and his mount sets off with him, standing, he will be deemed worthy of the race."
"15551","(15551) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked stones being stoned at night."
"15552","(15552) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he disliked throwing stones. At night"
"15553","(15553) Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, that Umm Salma ibn al-Mukhtar was under A son of Abdullah bin Omar. She was born in Muzdalifah, and Safiyyah was left behind with her. She did not miss that night and the next day, then They came to me during the night and stoned the burning coal, but Abdullah did not deny that to them, nor did he command them to make up for anything."
"15554","(15554) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Do not stone the stones at night."
"15555","(15555) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Pilgrims come forward and look after their backs, and they come and turn to the night."
"15556","(15556) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr, who said: Tell me about someone who saw some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. The stone is thrown at the setting of the sun, whether the sun has set, or has not set."
"15557","(15557) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos, who said: The herder if he does not find a shepherd, and the man if he Forgetting to stone stones at night."
"15558","(15558) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The herdsmen throw at night, but no They spend the night."
"15559","(15559) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not He remained standing in Muzdalifah until he reached a very high distance, then he pushed off before the sun rose."
"15560","(15560) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, who heard Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarubu’ informing about, Jubayr bin Al-Huwarith heard Abu Bakr while he was standing on a straw saying: O people, the morning has passed, O people. In the morning, then he pushed, and it was as if I was looking at his thighs exposed by what his camel was scratching with its crotch."
"15561","(15561) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athai, who said: The time of the push from Muzdalifah. Like the value of the morning prayer of a people who wake up with the morning prayer when the camels can see the places of their loofahs."
"15562","(15562) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The people of the Jahiliyyah used to push From Arafat before sunset and from Muzdalifah after its rising, so God delayed this and brought forward this. He delayed the day of Arafat until sunset. He arrived from Muzdalifah before sunrise."
"15563","(15563) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Al-Zubair stood waiting for a group and it turned clear, so Ibn Umar said: Waiting for the sun to rise Should I do the pre-Islamic one? So Ibn Umar pushed back, and the people pushed back with his push."
"15564","(15564) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah explained From summing the amount of prayers of travelers in the morning prayer."
"15565","(15565) Ibn Numayr and Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: I heard Ibn Al-Zubair says: It is part of the Sunnah of Hajj to pray, then stand in Muzdalifah after praying the Fajr prayer when the dawn flashes. So when it gives, it will be paid."
"15566","(15566) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Before sunrise."
"15567","(15567) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Al-Daf’ is from the plural of sunrise."
"15568","(15568) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Before sunrise."
"15569","(15569) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The amount of the morning prayer is no. Hastened, not delayed."
"15570","(15570) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He only made Circumambulating the Kaaba and striving between Safa and Marwah to establish the remembrance of Allah."
"15571","(15571) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 1883. Ahmad 6/139)"
"15572","(15572) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya Al-Qaisi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: The pebbles of the Jamarat are removed."
"15573","(15573) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, who said: I told Ibn Abbas, “Throw the stone in the Jahiliyah.” And Islam, and he said: Whatever is accepted from him will be removed, and had it not been for that, he would have been greater than Thabeer."
"15574","(15574) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he said regarding obligatory guidance: No. He will eat from it and he will be rewarded, and he said in voluntary prayers: He will eat from it."
"15575","(15575) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about the gift of a man who drove a camel and it became damaged. He said: “He eats.” He gives food and gives in charity because he has to pay."
"15576","(15576) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he brings an obligatory sacrifice and it becomes spoiled, he eats it. And he fed, and he owed an allowance."
"15577","(15577) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Eat and replace if it becomes damaged. The guidance, even if it is obligatory."
"15578","(15578) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Musa bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a body of eighteen people with a man, so he ordered him to do what he ordered about them, and he departed, then he came back and said to him: Have you seen? If anything from it creeps upon us? He said: Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood and place it on its surface, and do not eat from it, nor do you, nor anyone else. Your companions (Muslim 962. Abu Dawud 1760)"
"15579","(15579) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Najiya Al-Khuza’i, who said: I said, O Messenger of God, What do I do with what is damaged from the body? He said: Slaughter him, dip his sandals in his blood, and leave him alone among the people, so that they may eat him. \n(Ibn Majah 3106. Ahmad 4/334)"
"15580","(15580) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sinan bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Dhu’ayb Al-Khuza’i narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to send a body with him, and he said: If any of it is damaged and you fear death, slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then smack it on it. Leave it, and do not feed any of your companions from it. (Ibn Majah 3105. Ahmad 4/225)"
"15581","(15581) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Abdullah was sent with me to bring his body voluntarily, and it became damaged. On the way, she slaughtered it, gave some of it in charity, and returned to him with some of it, and he ate, but did not change it."
"15582","(15582) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he drives a sacrificial animal voluntarily and it becomes damaged? He said: Eat and be fed, and you do not have to change anything."
"15583","(15583) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Each of the voluntary acts, enjoyment, and guidance Al-Ihssar and vows if he does not say the name."
"15584","(15584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It is eaten from voluntary and tamattu’."
"15585","(15585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: voluntary charity, and prayer. And fasting and circumambulation, if he wishes, he may complete it, and if he wishes, he may interrupt it."
"15586","(15586) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan and his followers, and Ibn Sirin regarding the man who begins the circumambulation. Voluntarily, then he stops it. They said: He completes his tawaaf."
"15587","(15587) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you attend an prescribed prayer while you are circumambulating the Kaaba So interrupt your tawaaf, then pray, then complete the remainder of your tawaaf."
"15588","(15588) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: If you wish, pay off what remains, and if you wish So come forward."
"15589","(15589) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, that he was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and the prayer was performed. He prayed, then returned to Al-Safa and Al-Marwah and completed what remained."
"15590","(15590) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Mecca, who said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulating, and he The prayer was established, so he entered the prayer, and when he finished the prayer, he began his tawaf."
"15591","(15591) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he built Ali What remains?"
"15592","(15592) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he circumambulated five times, then The prayer was performed and he prayed. When he finished his prayer, he continued the remaining tawaf and prayed two rak’ahs."
"15593","(15593) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Dirham, who said: Mujahid sent me on a pilgrimage. While I was circumambulating the Kaaba with him, I said to him: I did not complete my circumambulation. He said: You should return and complete it."
"15594","(15594) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who was approached by a pilgrim who said: He should stop his tawaf and resume it."
"15595","(15595) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, that he used to present the custom of So he turns away from Arafat and does not come to the House."
"15596","(15596) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and “giving” in a man who comes alone and finds people standing. With his knowledge, they said: He will stand with them, so when it is the Day of Sacrifice he circumambulates once and runs between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa, so that is sufficient. The circumambulation of arrival is part of the circumambulation of the visit, and he must perform the circumambulation of the Day of Departure when he bids farewell to the House."
"15597","(15597) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he was asked about the one who performs qarin, and he said: I would love for someone to take the sacrificial animal from where it is in ihram."
"15598","(15598) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about a man who combined Hajj and Umrah, and he said: If he wishes, he can drive it, and if he wishes, it is sufficient for him to buy tea from Mecca."
"15599","(15599) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, that Shuraih and Al-Hussein bin Ali joined forces, but he did not guide them."
"15600","(15600) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I do not like the Qur’an, unless it is recited, and the one who enjoys it. It is sufficient for a sheep."
"15601","(15601) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salih al-Ukli, who said: I asked al-Sha’bi about the Qur’an, and he said: It is good, and they did not discuss it between the two of them. And I asked him about tamattu’, and he said: Good, and they did not get comfortable between them. I asked him about being alone, and he said: Good. I said: Yes. Do I admire you? He said: abstraction."
"15602","(15602) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The qiran and the mutati’ are sufficient. He bought them sheep from Mecca."
"15603","(15603) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The most beloved of things to him was for a person to make ihram. If it drives, and if it does not drive, then it does not surprise him."
"15604","(15604) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Some of our companions narrated to us that he asked Jabir bin Abdullah To combine Hajj and Umrah with something other than Hady, and he said: I have not seen any of us do that."
"15605","(15605) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, that he joined and bought A gift from Mecca"
"15606","(15606) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, that he hated to be associated with Unless he drives."
"15607","(15607) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Khasif, or Ali bin Bazimah, on the authority of Mujahid, in a similar manner."
"15608","(15608) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, that he hated to He stones the stones without performing ablution."
"15609","(15609) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muslim, on the authority of someone who heard Ata’ hate him to stone the stones without performing ablution. And if he does that, that is sufficient for him."
"15610","(15610) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to perform ablution when he stoned the Jamarat."
"15611","(15611) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They used to wash themselves when they went to the pebbles."
"15612","(15612) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked throwing stones at other than Ablution"
"15613","(15613) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: They used to wash themselves when they went to shoot stones."
"15614","(15614) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, that he used to wash himself when he went to The stones"
"15615","(15615) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I did not see Ibn Umar intending to stone the Jamarat except He took a bath."
"15616","(15616) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked, about a man who ran between the two rows. And Al-Marwah was mentioned fourteen times. He said: “Eid”."
"15617","(15617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is sufficient."
"15618","(15618) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He greeted the Yemeni Corner and placed his cheek on it."
"15619","(15619) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Amr bin Maymun receiving the pillar. The Yamani and places his cheek on it."
"15620","(15620) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: Whoever stands at Arafah will face the House."
"15621","(15621) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I told Nafi’, Ibn Umar was facing the house. In the situation he baptized? He said: Yes."
"15622","(15622) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode until The situation came and He made the belly of His she-camel close to the rocks, and He made the mountain of walkers between His hands, and He faced the direction and did not move. He stood until the sun set."
"15623","(15623) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah When he reached Jamrat al-Aqaba, he went further into the valley, faced the Ka’bah, and placed it on his right eyebrow, then stoned it with seven stones. Pebbles, he pronounces takbir with every pebble."
"15624","(15624) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, that he performed Hajj. With Abdullah and that he stoned the coals with seven pebbles and placed the House, on his left and on his right, then he said: This is the place of the One to whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed. (Bukhari 1747, Muslim 307)"
"15625","(15625) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, Mujahid, and Sa’id bin Jubayr. When they stoned the Jamarat, they would face the Ka’bah."
"15626","(15626) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I saw Ata, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, and Amr ibn Dinar standing, on the authority of Yassar al-Jamraiyah"
"15627","(15627) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, he said: Umar said: Whoever presents his weight to depart for the night will not perform Hajj. No"
"15628","(15628) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: If you travel, then do not Your weight precedes you, for that is undesirable."
"15629","(15629) Abu Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If it is permissible for you to flee, there is no harm in offering your burden."
"15630","(15630) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Omar, he said: Whoever presents his weight before departing, then there is no Hajj for him."
"15631","(15631) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Ammar bin Yasir, on the authority of Ammar said: If it is permissible for you to have a group, then give your weight if you wish."
"15632","(15632) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: If the Meccan departs for a certain time and enjoy So the guidance is upon him."
"15633","(15633) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The sacrifice is upon him, and Ata’ said: He is not upon him. Something"
"15634","(15634) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: If a Meccan enjoys the enjoyment, then no This is a gift for her."
"15635","(15635) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Waqaq ibn Iyas, on the authority of Quraysh, on the authority of Sa`sa`, he said: I heard a man ask Ibn Umar, and he said: Did she take an oath, or did her body be imposed on me, “Shall I slaughter it in the land in which I live?” He said: Do not slaughter her without the place of the body. The man said: I only said: Should I slaughter her in the land where I am? But Abdullah bin Omar refused, and said: Whoever wishes, Satan will make things beautiful for him."
"15636","(15636) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I mentioned to him what Ibn Umar said: He slaughtered her in Mecca and said: I did not feel it."
"15637","(15637) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Abd Al-Malik, on the authority of Ataa, they said: Whoever has his body assigned to him, then in Mecca, and if he says: A mountain, or a cow, then wherever he wants and wherever he intends."
"15638","(15638) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man places his body as his own, let him slaughter it wherever he names it. If he does not pronounce the poison, let him slaughter her in Mecca."
"15639","(15639) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Habib, who said: I heard Salim bin Abdullah and he was asked about the body. He said: My body will not be sufficient except in this city, meaning Mecca."
"15640","(15640) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr and Ikrimah, who said: No. A place for the body other than the ancient house."
"15641","(15641) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab about a man who puts a body on him. He said: He slaughters her wherever he wants and wherever he intends."
"15642","(15642) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Jahm al-Bakri, that a man vowed to sacrifice his body. In Kufa, he asked Ibn Masoud, and he said: Slaughter her wherever you want."
"15643","(15643) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabalah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Whoever names, or vows his body, let him A place for it other than the House, and whoever names a island or a cow, then wherever he wants."
"15644","(15644) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they said: What is your intention?"
"15645","(15645) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever sacrifices his body should only slaughter it for it. In Mina or Mecca, and whoever has sacrificed camels let him slaughter them wherever he wishes."
"15646","(15646) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Hasan, who said: If he said Ali is a guide, then in Mecca, and if he says: physically, then wherever he wants."
"15647","(15647) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimoon, who said: Whoever places a body burden on him, he will not We slaughter it except in Mecca, and whoever places a camel on it, he may slaughter it wherever he wants."
"15648","(15648) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When she took the vow of Umrah and was afraid She missed the Hajj, performed the Hajj, and completed the Umrah, and she must pay a sacrifice, and the Umrah is due."
"15649","(15649) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: I asked them, On the authority of a woman who came to Mecca for Umrah, then she had her period and was afraid that she would miss Hajj, so they said: She should perform the Hajj and perform it."
"15650","(15650) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who declared the ihram for his life, and he came while the people were standing by his side, and he said: If he knows that he is approaching Makkah, he will come to her, then he may enter from Umrah, otherwise he performs Hajj and performs two circumambulations."
"15651","(15651) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: You are a Rafidi. For the Umrah, and there is blood on it, and the Umrah is in its place."
"15652","(15652) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to recommend the Umrah of Muharram."
"15653","(15653) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I said to Salem bin Abdullah: The age of Muharram is a father. He said: Yes"
"15654","(15654) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Al-Qasim: What is the Umrah in Muharram? He said: They saw it as complete."
"15655","(15655) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I asked Suleiman bin Yasar And Salem bin Abdullah, about the life of Muharram, and they said: It is complete and must be made up."
"15656","(15656) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, who said: Tawoos was asked about the age of Muharram? He said: No, by Lord, I do not know what it is."
"15657","(15657) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Nāḥas ibn Qaym, on the authority of Ata`, that he used to prefer not to go out. From his tawaf except on Witr."
"15658","(15658) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Two tawafs are more beloved to me. From Tawaf."
"15659","(15659) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to disperse the night and the fire on Witr. From his tawaaf."
"15660","(15660) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to like to perform the Witr tawaf. Al-Hasan used to say: Ten days are more beloved to me than nine, and eight days are more beloved to me than seven."
"15661","(15661) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, that he used to say: Two tawaafs are more beloved to me than tawaaf."
"15662","(15662) Abu Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr roamed the leadership of Sa’id. So he went out to pray, and Abd al-Rahman said: Wait until he left for the Witr prayer. He said, wait for him. He said, then left for three tawafs, then he did not. He counts seven for that."
"15663","(15663) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Three weeks are more beloved to me than four."
"15664","(15664) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who circumambulated the Kaaba and forgot to sand, he said: He shed blood."
"15665","(15665) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he forgets to sand the three rounds, he will sand in the meantime. He remains, and if there is only one round left in which he sands, and nothing is due on him, then if he does not sand in any of them, then there is nothing. Aliyah"
"15666","(15666) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for a person to lean his back against someone. The Kaaba turns around."
"15667","(15667) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khalifa bin Khayyat, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he delivered a speech while leaning his back against the Kaaba. (Ahmad 2/191)"
"15668","(15668) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, in his saying: {That is for those whose family are not present in the mosque. The Sacred Mosque} He said: None are present at the Sacred Mosque except the people of the Sacred Mosque."
"15669","(15669) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The people of Fakh, the people of Dhanan, and the people of Arafah are them. His family"
"15670","(15670) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the sacrificial animal is difficult for you when you want to slaughter it So his neck"
"15671","(15671) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the body is difficult for you, then hinder it."
"15672","(15672) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not hamstring the body."
"15673","(15673) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The body should not be hamstrung."
"15674","(15674) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father used to bind the garment around his stomach, and he did not tie it. Muharram."
"15675","(15675) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos, who said: We saw Ibn Umar while he was in ihram and he had tied the knot. His loins are covered with a turban."
"15676","(15676) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Do not tie the knot. You owe something while you are in ihram."
"15677","(15677) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in tying a knot over a sore."
"15678","(15678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Hassan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He saw a man with a rope tied while he was in ihram, and he said: O owner of the rope, throw it. (Abu Dawud 158)"
"15679","(15679) Al-Ukli told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Khurasani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There is no problem. For the pilgrim in ihram to tie a knot over the wound."
"15680","(15680) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in bandaging a wound."
"15681","(15681) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him."
"15682","(15682) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the hand of a Muhrim is broken, and if he is injured, he should bandage it. Mansour said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"15683","(15683) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about a person who gives in Muharram and whose hand is broken. He said: Yes, and he wrapped a rag around her."
"15684","(15684) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I said to Jabir bin Zaid: Is my garment to be untied with my own knot, so should I tie it? He said: Yes."
"15685","(15685) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hujar, who said he saw a peacock of Ibn Umar roaming around with his loins girded. With a turban"
"15686","(15686) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, that she was asked, about Al-Himyan for the one in ihram, and she said: Bind your expenses around your loins."
"15687","(15687) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far and Ata’ about the intoxication of a person in ihram, and they said: There is no problem with it."
"15688","(15688) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no harm in a woman in ihram giving her wriqa."
"15689","(15689) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, who said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah about the rationale for ihram, and he said: No. He was beautiful with her, and I saw that he was wearing a flowing garment."
"15690","(15690) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no problem, even if it is difficult."
"15691","(15691) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he disliked it."
"15692","(15692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: There is no harm in him."
"15693","(15693) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Salih bin Jubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, that he was asked about A man who has a belt and ties it around his waist. He said: Yes, but he does not tie it around the neck of the loincloth."
"15694","(15694) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that he disliked the ihram for the ihram."
"15695","(15695) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Bakir, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in inattentiveness. For the mahram."
"15696","(15696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hamid al-Araj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no problem with him."
"15697","(15697) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He who wears hemian means the one in ihram."
"15698","(15698) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, that Ibn al-Zubayr came to perform Hajj and left for three. Circumambulating until I saw that his girdle on his stomach was cut off."
"15699","(15699) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he did not He considers it permissible for a pilgrim in ihram to wear the hemian if he is making ends meet in it."
"15700","(15700) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, he said: I asked Muhammad ibn Ka’b about him, and he said: He disagreed. According to the jurists, if you are strict, then good, and if you are relaxed, then good."
"15701","(15701) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in inattentiveness for a person in ihram. But the journey is not complicated for him, but rather he is wrapped around."
"15702","(15702) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: No one should exceed the time except one in ihram."
"15703","(15703) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: No one exceeds a single race even He is forbidden."
"15704","(15704) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said to him: If you come from another country, do not exceed the limit until You are forbidden."
"15705","(15705) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he used to say: The time should not exceed the time until you enter ihram."
"15706","(15706) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Ata used to make a concession regarding the penis, the siwak, and the tooth from the sanctuary."
"15707","(15707) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked it."
"15708","(15708) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The person in ihram should not leave the Sacred Mosque."
"15709","(15709) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Badhima, on the authority of a servant of Ibn Abbas, who said: I had fun but forgot to sacrifice I delayed my sacrifice until the days had passed, so I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: Give a gift for him and a gift for what you delayed."
"15710","(15710) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Rashid, he said: I asked Tawoos about a man. He enjoyed his fast and did not fast, nor did he slaughter until the days had passed. He said: He said: He would slaughter. I said: He could not find it. He said: He would sell his clothes. I said: He does not find it. He said: Let him borrow from his companions. I said: They will not give it to him. He said: I lied."
"15711","(15711) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, and Sa’id bin A splint in the case of a man who did tamattu but did not slaughter the animal and did not fast. He said, so they said: It is obligatory for him to sacrifice it."
"15712","(15712) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us on the authority of Habib, who said: Ata’ was asked about Umrah in other than the months of Hajj, for which there is a sacrifice. Obligatory? He said: There is no obligatory sacrifice in it, and they used to practice guidance, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, guided him when he stopped him. The polytheists, so was he in ihram for Umrah? He said: Yes, and he made an agreement with them that he would come to them in the next year, and I saw Mu’awiyah slaughtering a mountain in the age of Other than the months of Hajj."
"15713","(15713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he was trapped and slaughtered, he shaved his head."
"15714","(15714) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and said: The person in ihram kills the wolf. (Abu Dawud 1371; Abd al-Razzaq 8384)"
"15715","(15715) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Harmaliya, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted him and said: The person in ihram kills the wolf."
"15716","(15716) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The person in ihram kills the wolf."
"15717","(15717) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The person in ihram is killed. The wolf"
"15718","(15718) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Drive the wolf away from your mount while you Muharram."
"15719","(15719) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The person in ihram kills the wolf."
"15720","(15720) Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaysiyya bin Dhu’ayb, who said: The wolf is killed in The sanctuary"
"15721","(15721) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’ in Muharram kills a wolf and a lion, they said: Kill him, for he is an enemy."
"15722","(15722) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar, who said: The person in ihram is killed. The wolf and the snake."
"15723","(15723) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Kill the wolf and every enemy not mentioned in it. The book"
"15724","(15724) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, that a foreign woman came and performed all of the rituals. However, she did not perform the ihram for anything, so Ata’ said: It is not sufficient.\n Tawus said: It is sufficient. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it easy, and do not make it difficult.\n(Bukhari 69. Abu Dawud 4802)"
"15725","(15725) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, that a foreign man performed Hajj, but he did not call it Hajj, nor did he call it Hajj. Omar, and he said: I am with the people, and he said: I hope that he has entered into the best of what they have done."
"15726","(15726) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ka’b gave away imitation cows as a gift."
"15727","(15727) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Cows imitate, but do not perceive."
"15728","(15728) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to imitate cows and make them feel their hair. In its humps, and if it does not have a hump, then its place."
"15729","(15729) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid that they said: There is no life but his life. You started it from your family, and there is no life after the beginning, and Sa`id bin Jubayr said: If he returns to the appointed time of his land, he will be satisfied. I hope that You will be a woman"
"15730","(15730) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: We used to reach Medina with sacrificial meat."
"15731","(15731) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to not eat from the body except for a few days. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted us permission and said: Eat and provide for yourself. So we ate and provided for ourselves. He said: We said to Ataa: Do you think he was singled out? Is this the only means of enjoyment? He said: No, but I do not see it except the one completely guided. (Bukhari 2980, Muslim 30)"
"15732","(15732) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Nafi`, that Ibn Umar would not eat more than three meals."
"15733","(15733) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, that he said: No. Anyone can eat from his sacrifice of more than three."
"15734","(15734) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Bakhtari ibn Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I forbade you from the meat of sacrificial animals, so eat and provide for your travels."
"15735","(15735) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to take supplies to Medina on the authority of The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 2980, Muslim 1562)"
"15736","(15736) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We were landing. With the destinies."
"15737","(15737) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Anas, who said: We used to slaughter whatever God wished. We sacrificed it and ate the rest of it with basra."
"15738","(15738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the man who performs Hajj, on the authority of the man who did not perform Hajj, he said: It is sufficient."
"15739","(15739) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Indeed, God is sufficient for all of them."
"15740","(15740) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man performing Hajj, on the authority of the man, he said: He hopes for a reward similar to his."
"15741","(15741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was descending Wadi Nimra, and when Al-Hajjaj fought Ibn al-Zubayr, he sent a courier to me, who was the spirit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, on this day, he said: If that is the case, we will go. Then Al-Hajjaj sent a man, and he said: If he goes, let me know. Then Ibn al-Zubayr wanted to go, and they said: The sun had not risen, so he sat down. Then he wanted to go, and they said: The sun had not risen, so he sat down. Then when, They said: It has deviated, it has gone away. (Ahmed 25. Abu Dawud 1909)"
"15742","(15742) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Talq, who said: Omar said to Zayd bin Suhan, “Where is your home in Minna?” He said in the left part. He said: That is the abode of the dag, so do not go down to it. Amr said: And my abode is in it."
"15743","(15743) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, who said: They used to like to come down. The right side of Mina."
"15744","(15744) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was The right side descends from manna."
"15745","(15745) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, in his saying: {So whoever is hasty in Two days, there is no sin upon him. He said: He will be forgiven. {And whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.} He said: He will be forgiven."
"15746","(15746) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: (So whoever hastens In two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays it, there is no sin on him.) He said in hastening it, he said (and whoever delays), he said in Delay it"
"15747","(15747) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sawadah ibn Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said: He came away from his sins. Like the day his mother gave birth to him."
"15748","(15748) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya, who said: I heard Mujahid saying: {So whoever is hasty in two days, let him not It is a sin on him. He said: To Qabil. And whoever delays, there is no sin on him."
"15749","(15749) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: {So whoever is hasty in two days, let him Sin is upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.} He said about hastening it."
"15750","(15750) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He saw no harm in a man circumambulating the Kaaba. He makes two, then three times before running between Safa and Marwa."
"15751","(15751) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: When he bought a body, he would imitate it where He bought it in Mecca, or in Mina."
"15752","(15752) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to imitate the Day of Tarwiyah. And before that"
"15753","(15753) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, that Ibn al-Zubayr saw people cleaning the shrine, and he said: You were not commanded. With this, you were only commanded to pray there."
"15754","(15754) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not kiss the shrine, and do not touch it."
"15755","(15755) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he entered and did not pray, that is, in the house."
"15756","(15756) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered The Kaaba, so he stood at a pillar and called, but did not pray. (Bukhari 398. Ahmad 1/237)"
"15757","(15757) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, who said: I entered with Ali, Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein. And Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, the Ka`bah, so they did not pray in it."
"15758","(15758) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I entered the house with Omar bin Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafi, and he stood up and called, then He entered the house, then went out, and did not pray."
"15759","(15759) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’ in Muharram, who pointed to a hunter, and Muharram attacked him, saying: May the reward be upon him."
"15760","(15760) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, about the counselor, guide, and killer of every one of them. reward"
"15761","(15761) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I pointed to an antelope. I am in ihram and I hunt. He said: I am guaranteed."
"15762","(15762) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: A man said to Tawoos, “Did I indicate that it is permissible to hunt while I am in ihram?” He said: I guarantee."
"15763","(15763) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The pilgrim in ihram should not point to the game. And it does not indicate it."
"15764","(15764) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of a peacock like him."
"15765","(15765) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the pilgrim in ihram points to the game So you were stubborn, so he must make expiation."
"15766","(15766) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid, they said: If the forbidden commands the lawful By killing the game, he must make expiation."
"15767","(15767) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar, that Habbar is a man from the people of the Levant. He said: I came to Omar bin Al-Khattab while he was slaughtering a body in the slaughter house."
"15768","(15768) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The slaughterhouse in Mecca, but we It was cleansed of blood. He said: I said to Ataa: Where do you slaughter? He said on my journey."
"15769","(15769) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, that he He slaughters his camel on his journey."
"15770","(15770) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to slaughter in the slaughterhouse. He said: Servants of God: the slaughterhouse of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"15771","(15771) Khalid told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, that Salim was slaughtering his family."
"15772","(15772) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: He slaughters the body wherever it is convenient for him to do so. From me"
"15773","(15773) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: From all of it. A slope, and every entrance to Mecca is a slope."
"15774","(15774) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Abu Ja`far slaughtering camels in Mina at the slaughterhouse, and he did not He knows"
"15775","(15775) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Kharijiya bin Yazid slaughtering in his house. At Mina, and he did not slaughter in the slaughterhouse."
"15776","(15776) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah being slaughtered in The slope."
"15777","(15777) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to slaughter in Mecca. He said : Ibn Umar was slaughtering in Mina."
"15778","(15778) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Ibrahim slaughtered Al-Khalil behind Al-Aqba."
"15779","(15779) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I said to Ata’: Where should I sacrifice my sacrifice at the highest place in Mecca? Below? He said: Yes, I said: With the simplest? He said: Yes, I said: In my house? He said: Yes."
"15780","(15780) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to slaughter his goats behind his back. The obstacle"
"15781","(15781) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayash, on the authority of Zaid bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: From They are all slopes."
"15782","(15782) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir about a woman who forgot to cut her hair until she went out, and he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad and Aamir: cutting and shedding of blood."
"15783","(15783) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, about a man who forgot to shave, or cut his hair short, He said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"15784","(15784) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, Al-Qasim, Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid. In a woman who was passing by, returning from Mecca, and did not shorten her hair, they said: God will not hold her accountable for forgetfulness, and Ibn Al-Aswad said And Al-Shaabi: She cuts her hair while there is blood on her, and her Hajj is complete."
"15785","(15785) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who raised him, said: Do not tighten. Traveling is only to three mosques: the Grand Mosque, the Prophet’s Mosque, and Al-Aqsa Mosque."
"15786","(15786) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Talq, on the authority of Qaza’a, who said: I asked Ibn Umar whether he had come to Al-Tur? He said: Leave the mountain, do not come to it, and he said: Do not embark on a journey except to three mosques."
"15787","(15787) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Don’t set out on saddles except for three people. Mosques: The Grand Mosque, the Prophet’s Mosque, and Bayt al-Maqdis."
"15788","(15788) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: A man came to Umar and said: I I want the Holy House. So he said: Go and prepare yourself. When you are prepared, give me permission. When he was prepared, he came to you and said: Make it. A lifetime"
"15789","(15789) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id, who said: We saw Umar displaying the camels of charity when he came Two passengers, and he said: From where? They said: From the Holy House, and Omar gave them a stone. He said: A Hajj like the Hajj to the Holy House."
"15790","(15790) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: Do not set out on a saddle except To three mosques: the Grand Mosque, the Mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Aqsa Mosque."
"15791","(15791) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Dhayl, he said: Do not travel. Except to the ancient House."
"15792","(15792) Yahya bin Ya’li told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Do not embark on journeys except to three mosques: the Grand Mosque and the Mosque of the Messenger, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and Al-Aqsa Mosque."
"15793","(15793) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not travel except to three mosques: the Grand Mosque, the Al-Aqsa Mosque, And this mosque of mine."
"15794","(15794) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he imitated two sandals. (Tirmidhi 906 and Abu Dawud 1750)"
"15795","(15795) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to collect his sandals from the Sunnah. So he imitates her with his body, and if she is unable, he buys new shoes and imitates her."
"15796","(15796) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to imitate his physical appearance. Nalinin."
"15797","(15797) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Mukhlid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He imitated her ruins. Auction call"
"15798","(15798) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he once imitated a new, broken husband. A polytheist"
"15799","(15799) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Majlis, on the authority of Ibn Umar, similar to the hadith of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim."
"15800","(15800) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he informed him of the one who saw Omar. He bathes with his custom while wearing the robe."
"15801","(15801) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Ummar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, that he took a bath, then went to Arafah."
"15802","(15802) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he went to the Ma’rif, he would wash himself."
"15803","(15803) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Zaid, who said: Mujahid took a bath on the day he was recognized, and I was with him."
"15804","(15804) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, that his father was He takes a bath on the day of Arafah."
"15805","(15805) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Go to Arafat, and if it is at noon, So wash yourself if you find water, otherwise perform ablution."
"15806","(15806) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Washing on the day of He knew"
"15807","(15807) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: When Abdullah ran in the depths of the valley, he said: My Lord, forgive and have mercy. Indeed, You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"15808","(15808) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah similar to him."
"15809","(15809) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever Omar passed through the valley between the two rows, And he strove about it until he crossed it and said: My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"15810","(15810) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, that his father used to say, “While he was running between the ranks of Safa” And what is narrated is: Oh God, this is one and the same. If He completes it, God has completed it."
"15811","(15811) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah, On the authority of Umm Wald Shaybah, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, running between Safa and Marwa, and he said: The abatah is not interrupted except with a shaddah. (Ibn Majah 2987. Ahmad 6/404)"
"15812","(15812) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: O Lord, forgive and have mercy. And You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"15813","(15813) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: O Lord, forgive and have mercy. And You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"15814","(15814) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Hanash, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to do it.\n(Bayhaqi 95)"
"15815","(15815) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in entering Mecca at night."
"15816","(15816) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It will not harm you if you enter Mecca by day or night."
"15817","(15817) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I entered Mecca with Al-Qasim at night."
"15818","(15818) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like to come out of Kufa. by night and to enter Mecca by day."
"15819","(15819) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, that he entered Makkah at night."
"15820","(15820) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisn, on the authority of Salim that he entered Mecca during the day."
"15821","(15821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he entered Mecca during the day."
"15822","(15822) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, who said: I entered with Sa’id bin Jubayr in Mecca at night."
"15823","(15823) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, that his father used to enter Mecca at night"
"15824","(15824) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I asked Tawus about a man who entered Mecca at night, and he said: Isn't that cold spoils? So I asked Al-Qasim and Ata’ about that, but they saw no harm in it."
"15825","(15825) And Ali bin Hakim told me that Sa’id bin Jubayr came to Mecca at night and circumambulated, but we did not know about him, and he did That is Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
"15826","(15826) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I was leading the people in prayer during Ramadan, and while I was praying, I heard Omar saying “Allahu Akbar” at the door of the mosque. He came and performed Umrah and entered and I prayed behind me."
"15827","(15827) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Khalid bin Asid, on the authority of Muhrish al-Kaabi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah from al-Ji’ranah, and then in the morning With the scarabs, so when the sun had set, he went in the belly of a saraf until he reached the road."
"15828","(15828) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Salih ibn Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of a man called: Khaled, on the authority of a servant of theirs, On the authority of her grandmother, that Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came to Mecca at night, walked around, and then left."
"15829","(15829) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Khalid bin Asid, on the authority of Muhrish, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Umrah of the Ji’ran, then returned. To it are like rays of silver. He said: And I saw its appearance as if it were a silver bullion."
"15830","(15830) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, or Mujahid, who said: The contenter is the one who is content with what he has been sent. To Him, and the one who confronts you will ask you."
"15831","(15831) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, he said: Someone who heard Ibn Umar while he was in Manna told me, and recited these verses: {So eat from it. And feed the contented one and the one who is free.} He said: He said to a boy with him: This is the contented one who is content with what You have given him."
"15832","(15832) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Al-Qani’ is the people of Mecca, and Al-Mu’tarr is the one who visits you. So he asks you."
"15833","(15833) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The contented one is the one who is content with you, and the one who rejects He will show you himself, but he will not ask you."
"15834","(15834) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The contented one is the one who is begging, and the one who is in disrepair: the one who is physically disturbed."
"15835","(15835) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, about a man who threw a game in the ground while he was In the sanctuary, or is it permissible, and hunting in the sanctuary? He said: May his ransom be upon him."
"15836","(15836) Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he was asked about a man who shot game while he was in the Sacred Mosque and it came out of the water. The sanctuary and he died. He said: He is guaranteed. And when he shoots it in the sanctuary and the hunt is in the sanctuary, then he enters the sanctuary and dies, he said: No. Guaranteed"
"15837","(15837) Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Hammad, about a man who threw a game of game in the desert, and it fell into the Haram and died. He said: It amazes me that he doesn't eat it."
"15838","(15838) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a game animal is caught in the wild and enters the sanctuary and dies, then he said: No. He is to be eaten because he died in the Sacred Mosque, and he is not to be paid the funeral because he was made to die in the Sacred Mosque."
"15839","(15839) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When he throws If he throws a shot while it is in the sanctuary and hits it in the Sacred Mosque, he has committed blasphemy, and if he throws it in the fire and hits it in the Sacred Mosque, he has committed blasphemy."
"15840","(15840) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I went out with Alqamah to Mecca, and he did not even wash himself. They entered it."
"15841","(15841) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the pilgrim in ihram wishes, he may take a bath, and if he wishes, he may not take a bath."
"15842","(15842) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Tamar, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: He should bathe when entering ihram and pray. Two rak'ahs"
"15843","(15843) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiyy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Whenever they wanted to enter into ihram They took a bath."
"15844","(15844) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ata’, that it was a wonder for him to take a bath when entering the state of Ihram. And when he enters Mecca"
"15845","(15845) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to like it if they wanted to They are forbidden to wash themselves."
"15846","(15846) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he removed his shirt in the year of turmoil, then He answered the prayer and did not wash himself."
"15847","(15847) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is Sunnah for a man to bathe if he wants. To be forbidden. (Tirmidhi 830, Ibn Khuzaymah 2595)"
"15848","(15848) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Qais, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: If you enter ihram So he took a bath."
"15849","(15849) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he did not give up Bathing when entering ihram, and he commands that."
"15850","(15850) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Nafi’ whether Ibn Umar used to bathe when entering ihram? He said: He might have bathed, or he might have performed ablution."
"15851","(15851) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he took a bath when he entered Mecca."
"15852","(15852) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Washing on the day of the coming of Mecca"
"15853","(15853) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqamiya, Al-Aswad, and our companions used to stop. To Bir Maimun, they bathed there and put on their best clothes."
"15854","(15854) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar did not enter Mecca in Hajj, or Umrah until one performs ghusl with Dhu Tawa."
"15855","(15855) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to wash himself when he entered Mecca and commanded them to do so."
"15856","(15856) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad used to stone the Jamarat on the day of the battle. Then it returns to its heaviness with manna."
"15857","(15857) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Hudhali, who said: I said to Al-Zuhri: Is it permissible for a man to stone a hot coal? Al-Aqaba, then he returns to his home, then he walks to Mecca? He said: They would not return to their homes when they stoned the Jamarat, and if a man returned to his home because of a need or loss, Or a pilgrim. I hope that there will be no harm in him, God willing."
"15858","(15858) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah, regarding a lizard struck in Muharram. A handful of food."
"15859","(15859) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq, who said: We went out as pilgrims until, when we were on some path, a man among us stepped on foot. A lizard killed him while he was in Ihram, so Omar bin Al-Khattab came to judge him, and he said to him: Omar: Judge with me, so they ruled on him. A grandfather gathered the water and the trees, then he said: Omar: It will be judged by just people among you."
"15860","(15860) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ata’, who said about the lizard."
"15861","(15861) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that Omar was judged in the hyena. A ram."
"15862","(15862) Shabab told us on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Ghaz, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever kills a hyena while he is in a state of ihram, he must make a ransom."
"15863","(15863) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali regarding the hyena when he attacked Ali. The person in ihram, let him kill him, but if he kills him before he transgresses against you, then he must do a sinful act."
"15864","(15864) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A hyena is killed in the Sacred Mosque."
"15865","(15865) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made the hyena a game animal, and made a ram in it when it came to Muharram."
"15866","(15866) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ikrimah, in Muharram, he struck locusts, he said: He gives in charity. Very quickly"
"15867","(15867) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of ‘ata’ in the locusts: a handful, or a morsel."
"15868","(15868) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ka’b, that a locust passed by him and he struck it. With his whip, he took it and roasted it, and they told him, and he said: This is a mistake, and I judge myself for this dirham. Then Omar came and said: You, the people of Homs, have a wealth of money. Dates are better than locusts."
"15869","(15869) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, something like it, or something similar."
"15870","(15870) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah Al-Bariki, who said: Abdullah bin Omar was He says about locusts: a handful of food."
"15871","(15871) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, Ata’, Mujahid, and Tawoos that they are, They said: Concerning grasshoppers, lizards, locusts, and dwarfs. They said: If he kills them intentionally, he feeds them something, and if it is a mistake, then there is nothing on him. And he said: Amer, and Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad: He feeds something, whether by mistake, or intentionally."
"15872","(15872) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that a person in ihram struck locusts, so Abd Allah ruled against him. Ibn Omar and another man, and one of them ruled that he had broken a date and the other had broken it."
"15873","(15873) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a person in ihram being struck by locusts, and he said: A date is better than a locust."
"15874","(15874) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Concerning locusts and the like, and what is less. A handful of food."
"15875","(15875) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He was arrested from Food"
"15876","(15876) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, in a state of ihram he was killed. Lice, he said: He gives something in charity."
"15877","(15877) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, and Abi Hashim, who said: He gives charity. With something"
"15878","(15878) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, and he was asked about a person in ihram being killed. Lice, he said: He gives in charity a portion of it, or a handful of food."
"15879","(15879) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, in his saying, “It is the same as the one who is disobedient in it.” And the desert, he said: God created the same in it."
"15880","(15880) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The people of Mecca and others in the homes are equal."
"15881","(15881) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Sabit: {It is the same for the one who devotes himself to it and the one who leaves it} He said: The one who deserts it. He comes from Hajj and those who are staying are equal in the houses. They stay wherever they wish. No man leaves his house."
"15882","(15882) Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, who said: People in the house are equal."
"15883","(15883) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: His family and others are the same in him."
"15884","(15884) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that Aisha was hastening in Wadi Muhassir."
"15885","(15885) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdul Rahman, that when Ibn Umar came to Wadi Muhassir He struck his camel."
"15886","(15886) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abd Allah ibn Masoud Placed in Wadi Muhassir."
"15887","(15887) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he saw no harm in wasting Wadi Muhassir and Karaha in the Arafat Mountains."
"15888","(15888) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Dhar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Uqba, the client of Adlam ibn Na`imah al-Hadrami said that he was sent from a group with al-Husayn ibn Ali and did not proceed further, so when he came to Wadi Muhassir, he said: Shout with your voice, run with your feet, and strike with your whip. He was pushed into the valley until the ground leveled with him, and he emerged from The valley"
"15889","(15889) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar used to say:\nTo You do the worries and burdens of our enemies pass."
"15890","(15890) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Othman, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz being placed in a valley. Muhassir, and he is on a bardhun."
"15891","(15891) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muadh Abi Al-Ala’, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad being placed in Wadi Muhassir."
"15892","(15892) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put In Wadi Muhassir. (ترمذی ۸۸۶۔ احمد ۳/۳۳۲)"
"15893","(15893) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Asama bin Zayd, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted Afad, and the peace be upon him, and he commanded them to be calm, and he was placed in Wadi Muhassir. (Ahmed 5/208)"
"15894","(15894) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Miswar bin Makhramah, on the authority of Omar, that he was placed in a valley Mohsir."
"15895","(15895) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he was placed in a valley Mohsir."
"15896","(15896) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubaidah It was placed in Wadi Muhassir."
"15897","(15897) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: My father used to slaughter his camel while standing."
"15898","(15898) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, they said: The one who performs prayers is on four, And the Sawafin are on three."
"15899","(15899) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If Ibn Umar wanted to He slaughtered her daughter, so she stood on three feet, then we slaughtered her."
"15900","(15900) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ayman ibn Nabil Abi Imran, who said: I asked Tawoos about the words of God (Sawaf) He said: You must slaughter while standing."
"15901","(15901) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Mujahid, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the body We have made for you as a ritual. By God, there is good for you in it, so mention the name of God over it in rows. He said: When we slaughter it while standing."
"15902","(15902) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Umar, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I saw Ibn Umar after he grew up. He will slaughter it, blessing you."
"15903","(15903) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If He wills, He will rise, and if He wills, He will bless it."
"15904","(15904) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he slaughtered it while standing."
"15905","(15905) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the verse: {So mention the name of May God be pleased with her. He said: Standing."
"15906","(15906) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of those mentioned, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He saw a man slaughtering his camel. Bless him: He said: Standing according to the Sunnah of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"15907","(15907) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that Ibn Umar used to slaughter it as a young man standing, and when he grew up, he slaughtered it. And He has blessed you."
"15908","(15908) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will slaughter her while I am blessing her. It will be easy for her and Ali. Who will slaughter her?"
"15909","(15909) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, that Ibn Umar came upon a man who had had intercourse with his body. He said: Slaughter her standing according to the Sunnah of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 1713 and Abu Dawud 1765)"
"15910","(15910) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he slaughtered three of his bodies. Standing up"
"15911","(15911) Shababi told us, he said: Ruqaqa told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr slaughtering her and A reasonable standing is one of her hands."
"15912","(15912) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Shaving and taking from the moustache. And trimming the nails and plucking the armpits."
"15913","(15913) Al-Ukli narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, who said: Al-Taftif means shaving the pubic hair and plucking it. The armpit, removing the mustache, and trimming the nails."
"15914","(15914) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Shaving, slaughtering, cutting the nails, and the rituals of Hajj."
"15915","(15915) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: They do not have to do the rituals."
"15916","(15916) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Hair and nails."
"15917","(15917) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Taftuf: archery, slaughter, and shaving. And trimming, and taking from the moustache, nails, and beard."
"15918","(15918) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, Hajj every year or every year. One? He said: No, rather he ordered it, so whoever increases it voluntarily. (Abu Dawud 1718, Darami 1789)"
"15919","(15919) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas, that A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Hajj every year, or once? He said: bitterly, or something like this.\n(Ibn Majah 2885)"
"15920","(15920) Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: They believed that the most knowledgeable of people about rituals was Ibn Affan, then After him, Ibn Umar."
"15921","(15921) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saif, on the authority of Aisha, that she said Ibn Abbas is the most knowledgeable of those who remain in Hajj."
"15922","(15922) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, who said: I was sitting with Abu Ja’far when Ata’ passed by, and Abu Jafar: There is no one more knowledgeable about the rituals of Hajj than a gift on the face of the earth."
"15923","(15923) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: It is Sunnah to ascend the Safa. Until the house appears to you and you receive it."
"15924","(15924) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He ascends Safa until he faces the House."
"15925","(15925) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he ascended al-Safa, he would face house and said “Allahu Akbar” three times, and said: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, to Him is praise, and He is above all. Something powerful, he raises his voice with it, then makes a long supplication."
"15926","(15926) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he rises upon As-Safa, he will stand on it. He sees the House from him."
"15927","(15927) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited a prayer for him until He saw the house."
"15928","(15928) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to stand on Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, where one sees the House."
"15929","(15929) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abdullah, that Salim ascended al-Safa to a place from which he could see the House."
"15930","(15930) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: He should not enter into ihram for Hajj on the day of Tarwiyah. Until he heads to Mina."
"15931","(15931) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr came out on the day of the Tarwiyah. He was walking and I went out with him, so he entered the mosque and prayed two rak’ahs, then he left the mosque and performed the prayer when he turned."
"15932","(15932) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Kaysan, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: It will not harm you, O people of Mecca, if you do not perform Umrah. If you refuse, then put the middle of the valley between you and the Sacred Mosque."
"15933","(15933) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The people of Mecca go out for Umrah. And they welcome the Hajj from their place."
"15934","(15934) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Khalid bin Muslim, on the authority of Salem, who said: If I was one of the people of Mecca as long as I performed Umrah."
"15935","(15935) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The people of Mecca do not have to perform Umrah. He only performs Umrah. Whoever visits the House may circumambulate it, and the people of Mecca circumambulate it whenever they wish."
"15936","(15936) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The people of Mecca do not have to pay a lifetime. Ibn Abbas: You, O people of Mecca, do not have a Umrah. Your Umrah is only the circumambulation of the House. Whoever puts a belly between him and the Sacred Mosque. A valley, so no one can enter Mecca except in a state of ihram. He said: So I said to Ata’: Does Ibn Abbas want the inner part of a valley to be permissible? He said: The belly of a valley of solitude."
"15937","(15937) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The people of Mecca are not Omar"
"15938","(15938) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: None of the people of Mecca is required to entertain."
"15939","(15939) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: The people of Mecca are not required to enjoy They are not required to circumambulate the House."
"15940","(15940) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The people of Mecca do not have to suffer."
"15941","(15941) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The people of Mecca are not required to do so. Enjoyment, then he recited: {That is for those whose family are not present at the Sacred Mosque}. If they do so, then perform the Hajj, then they will do the same as before. On the people"
"15942","(15942) Omar bin Ayyub Al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: It is not for the people of Mecca. And whoever looks at Mecca will not enjoy it."
"15943","(15943) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The person who provides entertainment for the people. All of them except the people of Mecca."
"15944","(15944) Shababih narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The people of Mecca are not required to enjoy, nor Ihsar, they only cheat until they complete their Hajj."
"15945","(15945) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, regarding his saying {Whoever finds a way to Him} He said: Whoever has provisions and camels, Hajj is obligatory for him."
"15946","(15946) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja’far, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A man rose To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, what makes Hajj obligatory? He said: Zad and his camels. He said: O Messenger of God, what is the Hajj? He said: The spittle, he said: Then he said: O Messenger of God, what is the best Hajj? He said: Al-Ajj and Al-Thajj. He said: Al-Ajj means the talbiyah, and Al-Thajj is the slaughter of the body."
"15947","(15947) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {Whoever is able To Him is a way.} He said: provision and camel."
"15948","(15948) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid Abi Karimah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Power On the strength of power."
"15949","(15949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding his saying: {Whoever is able to do so} he said: Produce and camels."
"15950","(15950) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Al-Zad And the departed one (Ibn Jarir 16)"
"15951","(15951) Abdul-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar thing."
"15952","(15952) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: {Whoever is able to find a way} He said: The way: provision and means of travel."
"15953","(15953) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Omar said: {Whoever is able to find a way} He said: Zad And his departure, and Ibn Abbas said: He who finds a way, but it is not permissible between him and her, and Ata’ said: A way, as God said."
"15954","(15954) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He provided and came back."
"15955","(15955) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Zad and his camels."
"15956","(15956) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, with a similar story."
"15957","(15957) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, a man said: O Messenger of God, what is the way to him? He said: Provision and food."
"15958","(15958) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, called: Khalid, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr: {Whoever is able To Him is a way} He said: According to the measure of strength."
"15959","(15959) Waki’ told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Who owned Three hundred dirhams, the Hajj is obligatory for him, and it is forbidden for him to marry female slaves."
"15960","(15960) Saeed bin Khathim narrated to us, on the authority of his brother Muammar bin Khathim, on the authority of Abu Jafar, he said: I said to him: May God have mercy on you. {Whoever can find a way to it} So what is the way? He said: To have a mount and a few provisions to walk on one's back and ride on one's back."
"15961","(15961) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, about a man presenting He was in Mecca on the day he was recognized as having performed Umrah, circumambulating the Kaaba and performing Safi between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa. He said: He should not come to women while people are standing. By knowledge"
"15962","(15962) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him."
"15963","(15963) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman in ihram must wear socks and trousers."
"15964","(15964) Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: Ata was asked: Should a woman in ihram wear trousers? He said: Yes."
"15965","(15965) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is no harm in wearing a mahram. Socks and trousers."
"15966","(15966) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Salama bin Wharam, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The woman in ihram wears trousers."
"15967","(15967) Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The woman in ihram must wear socks, trousers, and gloves. And it covers her entire face."
"15968","(15968) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata, who said: The woman in ihram wears trousers."
"15969","(15969) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to make a concession in socks. And trousers are for a woman in ihram. He said: Safiyya used to wear a woman’s socks while she was in a state of ihram, socks up to her knees."
"15970","(15970) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not think it was wrong for a woman to wear a mahram. The socks that are driven."
"15971","(15971) Affan told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Humaid al-Araj told us, on the authority of Mujahid, that Abdullah bin Amr, Abdullah bin Abbas, and Abdullah bin Omar, when they had completed their circumambulation and wanted to leave, they would return to the Rukn. And the door, or between the stone and the door."
"15972","(15972) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abi Dhubab, he said: Ikrimah told me, he said: Every hunter If a person in ihram takes it without the pigeon, it will pay its price."
"15973","(15973) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata that they did not see any harm in wearing Ihram. With a shirt."
"15974","(15974) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he hated it. That"
"15975","(15975) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majlis, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas stoning the Jamarat while he was fasting."
"15976","(15976) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she used to fast on the days of Tashreeq."
"15977","(15977) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he used to fast on the days of the East."
"15978","(15978) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Qays ibn Abaya, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about fasting. The day after the sacrifice, he said: Fast if you wish."
"15979","(15979) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he used to fast on the days of the East."
"15980","(15980) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hasan, who said: There is not a single day that I fast on. It is more beloved to me than fasting on the Day of New Years."
"15981","(15981) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn Umar: What kills a muhrim? He said: One of the wives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He ordered the killing of the crow."
"15982","(15982) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: The person in ihram kills the crow."
"15983","(15983) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, who said: I saw Ibn Umar throwing a crow. On the back of his camel while he was in ihram."
"15984","(15984) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul Al-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: Omar ordered us to kill the crow and the hornet while we were in ihram."
"15985","(15985) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Adam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: Stone the crow while you Muharram."
"15986","(15986) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I asked Mujahid about what they were killing in the Sacred Mosque, and he said: Al-Hayat. And the crow throws it."
"15987","(15987) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The person in ihram throws the crow."
"15988","(15988) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: The crow is killed."
"15989","(15989) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he greeted: for the person in ihram to kill the crow."
"15990","(15990) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qaz’a al-Balili, on the authority of Muhajir al-Makki, who said: A man asked Jabir bin Abdullah: Does one of us raise his hand when he sees the House? He said: That is the work of the Jews. We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we did not do that. (Abu Dawud 1845, Dharmi 1920)"
"15991","(15991) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qaz’a al-Baili, on the authority of Muhajir al-Makki, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah, does a man raise his hand when he sees the House? He said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we used to perform it."
"15992","(15992) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The hands are raised in Seven times, when he sees the House, and at Safa and Marwah and in the plural, and at the Arafat, and at the Jamarat."
"15993","(15993) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Munkadir, who said: No Hajj has ever performed the most brilliant Hajj, meaning as long as he is poor."
"15994","(15994) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Abdullah’s companions used to say: The hands should be raised in Eight places at the House, at Safa and Marwa, at Arafat, at Muzdalifah, and at the two Jamaratina."
"15995","(15995) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim and Khaythami, who said: It is raised during prayer, and when The House, and on Safa and Marwah and in Muzdalif."
"15996","(15996) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not raised. hands except in seven situations: when you stand for prayer, if you come from a land, if you see the House, and when you stand Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and at Arafat, and in a group, and at the Jamarat."
"15997","(15997) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The first time you enter Mecca, then You came to the stone, so thank God for His good facilitation and communication."
"15998","(15998) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Saeed - meaning: Muhammad bin Saeed -, on the authority of His father was happy because whenever he saw the House, he would say: Oh God, you are peace and from you is peace, so grant us peace, our Lord, with peace."
"15999","(15999) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man from the Levant, on the authority of Makhoul, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he saw the House, he said: O God, increase this House in honor, reverence, and majesty, and increase those who perform Hajj or Umrah on it. Honor, glorification, magnification, and righteousness. (Tabarani 3053)"
"16000","(16000) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sa’id, on the authority of his father, that when Omar entered the house, he said: Oh God, you are peace, and from you is peace, so grant us peace, our Lord."
"16001","(16001) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Muhammad bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that When he entered the Kaaba Mosque and looked at the House, he would say: O God, you are peace and from you is peace, so greet us with peace, our Lord."
"16002","(16002) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: My heart desires to die before I perform Hajj on foot."
"16003","(16003) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, that Abraham and Ismail performed Hajj. And they were walking."
"16004","(16004) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Hussein bin Ali performed Hajj on foot, and his journeys were led. Next to him, Hafs said: I count it, he said: Ten times."
"16005","(16005) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, who said: I saw Nafi’ ibn Jubayr judge He performs rituals on his feet, and he introduces himself to his feet."
"16006","(16006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I performed Hajj with Sa’id bin Jubayr, walking."
"16007","(16007) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Nafi’ whether Ibn Umar performed Hajj on foot? He said: No."
"16008","(16008) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Every time a muhrim strikes a hunter forgetfully, he will be punished."
"16009","(16009) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whenever a muhrim kills game, he will be punished."
"16010","(16010) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: A man asked him, and he said: I was correct. He was hunting while I was in ihram, so Shurayh said to him: Have you been infected before? He said: No. He said: If you had done so, I would have entrusted you to God Almighty until He takes revenge on you. {And God is Mighty, Possessor of Vengeance} David said: So I mentioned that to Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: Will he be removed and be judged?"
"16011","(16011) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If someone afflicts something, he will be judged. Then if he returns, he will not be judged. Then he recited: (And whoever returns, God will take revenge on him.)"
"16012","(16012) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him, saying: I will continue your Umrah and Hajj."
"16013","(16013) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bukair ibn Ata, on the authority of Harith ibn Sulaym, he said: I heard Ali He responded to Hajj and Umrah, so he began to perform Umrah, and Othman said to him: You are among those who will be looked at. Ali said to him: And you are among those He looks at her."
"16014","(16014) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: Here you are. With Umrah and Hajj."
"16015","(16015) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Ibrahim and Mujahid about a man who recites the Talbiyah. With Hajj and Umrah, and he said: Mujahid: He begins with Umrah, and he said: Ibrahim: The intention is sufficient."
"16016","(16016) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man begs for something with violets, he must pay a ransom."
"16017","(16017) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he gave a speech and said: If the person in ihram does not find a garment, then he should wear trousers, and if he does not find sandals, he should wear trousers. Let him wear socks.\n(Muslim 835. Bukhari 1740)"
"16018","(16018) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted with something like it, or something similar. (Muslim 835. Ahmad 1/221)"
"16019","(16019) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: (Muslim 825, Tirmidhi 834)"
"16020","(16020) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace What clothes should a person in ihram wear, or what should a person in ihram leave behind? He said: He should not wear socks or trousers, unless he cannot find sandals. Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear them. The socks and let him cut them below the ankles."
"16021","(16021) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever cannot find sandals should wear socks, and whoever cannot find a loincloth should wear trousers.\n(Muslim 836. Ahmad 3/323)"
"16022","(16022) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Yunus bin Saif, on the authority of Umair bin Al-Aswad, who said: I asked Omar, I said: What do you say about the socks for a person in ihram? He said: They are the sandals of someone who has no sandals."
"16023","(16023) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali in the state of Ihram if he did not find two sandals to wear He should wear socks, and if he does not find a loincloth, he should wear trousers."
"16024","(16024) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If If the person in ihram finds a garment, he should wear trousers, and if he does not find sandals, he should wear socks."
"16025","(16025) It was narrated to us that Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: If the person in ihram does not find a garment, let him wear it. Pants"
"16026","(16026) Abu Bakr told us, Ibn Numayr said, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in wearing ihram clothing. Trousers if he does not find a loincloth, and there is no harm in wearing slippers if he does not find sandals."
"16027","(16027) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: : Indeed, if I had come forward from my affair, I would not have turned back. I would not have given the animal to drink and made it a lifetime. So whoever of you does not have a sacrificial animal with him? So let him be permissible, and let him make it a lifetime. Then Suraqi stood up and said: O Messenger of God, is this for our time, or forever? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, interlocked his fingers one with the other and said: The Umrah has entered the Hajj, indeed forever. Forever"
"16028","(16028) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The people came with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted the pilgrims, so he ordered them to make it an ‘Umrah. Then he said: If I had accepted from my command, I would not have turned around, I would not have done that, but The Umrah began Hajj until the Day of Resurrection, then he interlaced his fingers. (Abu Dawud 1789. Tirmidhi 932)"
"16029","(16029) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace in the Hajj and make us join him. When we came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever was not with him A Hadi, let him be permissible, and he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as a Hadi, but he was not permissible. (Bukhari 4354, Muslim 185)"
"16030","(16030) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who were sluggish with Hajj during the months and days of Hajj, until we presented an extravagance, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He greeted his companions: Whoever among you has not brought a sacrifice and would like to complete the Ihram for Hajj during his ‘Umrah, let him do so."
"16031","(16031) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he said: This is a life we have enjoyed, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him may make it permissible in its entirety, as he has The Umrah began Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 203. Abu Dawud 1787)"
"16032","(16032) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: Mut’a was a special part of the Hajj for the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
